<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Pseudocodes for <span id="A1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Greedy Sampling</span> and <span id="A1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Explore-Then-Commit</span></h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Greedy Sampling</span></figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.6.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="alg1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Exploration policy <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
          Initialize <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}_{1}\leftarrow\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}_{1}\leftarrow\rho</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
          <span id="alg1.6.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg1.6.3.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\cdots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\cdots,T</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.6.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
          Observe a <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
          Sample <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{1}}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}(\cdot|{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒂</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{1}}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}(\cdot|{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{2}}\sim\rho(\cdot|{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒂</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{2}}\sim\rho(\cdot|{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
          Observe <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{t}:=\mathds{1}[{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{1}}\succ{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{2}}]\sim\mathrm{Ber}(\mu({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\phi_{t}^{1}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{\star}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\phi_{t}^{2}})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒂</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒂</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>Ber</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}:=\mathds{1}[{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{1}}\succ{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{2}}]\sim\mathrm{Ber}(\mu({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\phi_{t}^{1}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{\star}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\phi_{t}^{2}})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}^{i}:=\phi({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}_{t}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}^{i}:=\phi({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}_{t}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
          Compute an estimator <math id="alg1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d)</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
           <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
          Compute a (symmetric) Nash equilibrium:

<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}_{t+1}\leftarrow\argmax_{\pi^{1}\in\Pi}\min_{\pi^{2}\in\Pi}J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\pi^{2};\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}_{t+1}\leftarrow\argmax_{\pi^{1}\in\Pi}\min_{\pi^{2}\in\Pi}J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\pi^{2};\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.9" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> <span id="alg2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Explore-Then-Commit</span></figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.6.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="alg2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Exploration policy <math id="alg2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and budget <math id="alg2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
          <span id="alg2.6.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg2.6.2.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\cdots,T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\cdots,T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg2.6.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
          Observe a <math id="alg2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
          Sample <math id="alg2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{1}}\sim\rho(\cdot|{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒂</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{1}}\sim\rho(\cdot|{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{2}}\sim\rho(\cdot|{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒂</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{2}}\sim\rho(\cdot|{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
          Observe <math id="alg2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{t}:=\mathds{1}[{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{1}}\succ{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{2}}]\sim\mathrm{Ber}(\mu({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\phi_{t}^{1}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{\star}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\phi_{t}^{2}})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒂</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒂</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>Ber</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}:=\mathds{1}[{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{1}}\succ{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bm{a}}_{t}^{2}}]\sim\mathrm{Ber}(\mu({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\phi_{t}^{1}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{\star}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\phi_{t}^{2}})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="alg2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}^{i}:=\phi({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}_{t}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}^{i}:=\phi({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}_{t}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
          Compute an estimator <math id="alg2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d)</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
          Compute a (symmetric) Nash equilibrium:

<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}\leftarrow\argmax_{\pi^{1}\in\Pi}\min_{\pi^{2}\in\Pi}J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\pi^{2};\widehat{\bm{\Theta}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}\leftarrow\argmax_{\pi^{1}\in\Pi}\min_{\pi^{2}\in\Pi}J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\pi^{2};\widehat{\bm{\Theta}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
          <span id="alg2.6.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg2.6.8.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T_{0}+1,\cdots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T_{0}+1,\cdots,T</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg2.6.8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
          Symmetrically commit to <math id="alg2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\pi},\hat{\pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\pi},\hat{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.10" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1 Norm + Skew-Constrained MLE ‣ 4 𝒪̃⁢(𝜂⁢(log𝑇)^2∧√𝑇) via Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>: Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Main Proof</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will use several properties of the Kronecker product <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> throughout the proof; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib124" title="" class="ltx_ref">Minka (1997)</a></cite> for a reference.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part I. <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta(\log T)^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta(\log T)^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> Regret Bound.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To mirror the proof sketch in the main text, we divide the proof into three parts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1. From Regret to Sum of Squared Errors.</span>
Recall that with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{t}:=\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{2}(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{1})^{\top})\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{t}:=\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{2}(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{1})^{\top})\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, our MLE is defined as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}\leftarrow\mathrm{mat}(\hat{{\bm{\theta}}}_{t}),\quad\hat{{\bm{\theta}}}_{t}\leftarrow\argmin_{{\bm{\theta}}\in{\mathcal{K}}_{S}}{\mathcal{L}}_{t}({\bm{\theta}}),\quad{\mathcal{L}}_{t}({\bm{\theta}}):=\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\left\{m(\langle{\bm{\theta}},{\bm{v}}_{t}\rangle)-r_{t}\langle{\bm{\theta}},{\bm{v}}_{t}\rangle\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>mat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}\leftarrow\mathrm{mat}(\hat{{\bm{\theta}}}_{t}),\quad\hat{{\bm{\theta}}}_{t}\leftarrow\argmin_{{\bm{\theta}}\in{\mathcal{K}}_{S}}{\mathcal{L}}_{t}({\bm{\theta}}),\quad{\mathcal{L}}_{t}({\bm{\theta}}):=\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\left\{m(\langle{\bm{\theta}},{\bm{v}}_{t}\rangle)-r_{t}\langle{\bm{\theta}},{\bm{v}}_{t}\rangle\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{S}:=\left\{{\bm{\theta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{2}}:\left\lVert{\bm{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}\leq S\text{ and }\mathrm{mat}({\bm{\theta}})^{\top}=-\mathrm{mat}({\bm{\theta}})\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>mat</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>mat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{S}:=\left\{{\bm{\theta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{2}}:\left\lVert{\bm{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}\leq S\text{ and }\mathrm{mat}({\bm{\theta}})^{\top}=-\mathrm{mat}({\bm{\theta}})\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(z)=(1+e^{-z})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(z)=(1+e^{-z})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for our proof, this implies that <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{s}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{s}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mu}=\frac{1}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mu}=\frac{1}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let us denote the regularized Hessian of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{t}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{t}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> at the MLE <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{\theta}}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{\theta}}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}:={\bm{I}}_{d^{2}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\dot{\mu}(\langle\hat{{\bm{\theta}}}_{t},{\bm{v}}_{t}\rangle){\bm{v}}_{t}{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}:={\bm{I}}_{d^{2}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\dot{\mu}(\langle\hat{{\bm{\theta}}}_{t},{\bm{v}}_{t}\rangle){\bm{v}}_{t}{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We first recall the following elliptical confidence sequence:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem 3.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al. (2024a)</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any adaptively collected<span id="footnote9" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">9</span></span>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  <span id="footnote9.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">This can be formalized via the canonical bandit model as described in </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib102" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lattimore and Szepesvári (2020, Chapter 4.6)</a></cite><span id="footnote9.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span></span></span> <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{({\bm{v}}_{t},r_{t})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{({\bm{v}}_{t},r_{t})\}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\left\lVert{\bm{\theta}}_{\star}-\hat{{\bm{\theta}}}_{t}\right\rVert_{\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}}^{2}\lesssim\gamma_{t}(\delta),\ \ \forall t\geq 1\right)\geq 1-\delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≲</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\left\lVert{\bm{\theta}}_{\star}-\hat{{\bm{\theta}}}_{t}\right\rVert_{\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}}^{2}\lesssim\gamma_{t}(\delta),\ \ \forall t\geq 1\right)\geq 1-\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}(\delta)\lesssim S^{5}+S\log\frac{1}{\delta}+Sd^{2}\log\frac{St}{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}(\delta)\lesssim S^{5}+S\log\frac{1}{\delta}+Sd^{2}\log\frac{St}{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We note that this is used solely for the proof and does not affect the algorithm in any way.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">From the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent bound of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3 A New Analysis of Regularized Regret ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we have that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)\leq(L_{\mu}^{2}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta+L_{\mu})\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)\leq(L_{\mu}^{2}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta+L_{\mu})\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We decompose the squared Euclidean norm as follows:
denoting <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{e}}_{j}\}_{j\in[d]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{e}}_{j}\}_{j\in[d]}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the standard basis of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{d}\left({\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{d}\left({\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{d}\left(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{E}}_{t}{\bm{e}}_{j}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{d}\left(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{E}}_{t}{\bm{e}}_{j}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{E}}_{t}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{E}}_{t}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d)</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{d}\langle\mathrm{vec}({\bm{E}}_{t}),\mathrm{vec}({\bm{e}}_{j}\bm{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{d}\langle\mathrm{vec}({\bm{E}}_{t}),\mathrm{vec}({\bm{e}}_{j}\bm{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{d}\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}({\bm{E}}_{t})\right\rVert_{\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}}^{2}\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}({\bm{e}}_{j}\bm{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\right\rVert_{\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}^{-1}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{d}\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}({\bm{E}}_{t})\right\rVert_{\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}}^{2}\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}({\bm{e}}_{j}\bm{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\right\rVert_{\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}^{-1}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Cauchy-Schwarz)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\gamma_{t}(\delta)^{2}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\left\lVert\bm{\phi}_{t}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j}\right\rVert_{\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}^{-1}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\gamma_{t}(\delta)^{2}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\left\lVert\bm{\phi}_{t}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j}\right\rVert_{\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}^{-1}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Theorem 3.2 of ( ) ). ‣ Part I. 𝒪̃⁢(𝜂⁢𝛽⁢(log𝑇)^2) Regret Bound. ‣ B.1 Main Proof ‣ Appendix B Proof of : Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2. Towards Expected Elliptical Potentials.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We now present our key technical lemma:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="114.66" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 114.66" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,114.66) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 108.75 C 0 112.01 2.64 114.66 5.91 114.66 L 471.47 114.66 C 474.73 114.66 477.38 112.01 477.38 108.75 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 108.75 C 1.97 110.93 3.73 112.69 5.91 112.69 L 471.47 112.69 C 473.65 112.69 475.41 110.93 475.41 108.75 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 91.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:5.6em;font-size:10pt;" height="87.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Coverage Lemma)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]\succeq C_{\min}{\bm{I}}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⪰</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐈</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]\succeq C_{\min}{\bm{I}}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Then, for any positive semi-definite <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d^{2}\times d^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐌</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d^{2}\times d^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and any vector <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\phi}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\phi}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following holds:</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{d}(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})^{\top}{\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})\leq C_{\min}^{-1}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒆</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒆</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{d}(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})^{\top}{\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})\leq C_{\min}^{-1}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">From hereon, we denote <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{t-1}[\cdot]\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t},\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}\sim\rho}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{t-1}[\cdot]\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t},\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}\sim\rho}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is to indicate that the expectation is conditional on the history, due to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> being history-dependent.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Applying the above lemma with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}=\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}=\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\eta\beta d^{2}C_{\min}^{-1}\log\frac{T}{d}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}_{t}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}^{\top})^{\top}\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}^{-1}\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}_{t}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}^{\top})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\eta\beta d^{2}C_{\min}^{-1}\log\frac{T}{d}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}_{t}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}^{\top})^{\top}\widehat{{\bm{H}}}_{t}^{-1}\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}_{t}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}^{\top})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\eta\beta\kappa^{-1}d^{2}C_{\min}^{-1}\log\frac{T}{d}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}_{t}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}^{\top})^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}_{t}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}^{\top})\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\eta\beta\kappa^{-1}d^{2}C_{\min}^{-1}\log\frac{T}{d}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}_{t}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}^{\top})^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\phi}_{t}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}^{\top})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.2" class="ltx_p">where we have bounded <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}(\delta)^{2}\leq\gamma_{T}(\delta)^{2}\lesssim d^{2}\log\frac{T}{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}(\delta)^{2}\leq\gamma_{T}(\delta)^{2}\lesssim d^{2}\log\frac{T}{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we denote <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{t}=\bm{\phi}_{t}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{t}=\bm{\phi}_{t}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}_{t}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}_{t}:=\frac{1}{\kappa\wedge 1}{\bm{I}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}{\bm{v}}_{s}{\bm{v}}_{s}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}_{t}:=\frac{1}{\kappa\wedge 1}{\bm{I}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}{\bm{v}}_{s}{\bm{v}}_{s}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3. Martingale Concentration for Realized Variance.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">We now consider the elliptical-type quantity:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}\right]}_{\triangleq{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">T</mi></msub></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}\right]}_{\triangleq{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\underbrace{\left(\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}\right]-{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}\right)}_{\triangleq M_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\underbrace{\left(\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}\right]-{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}\right)}_{\triangleq M_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}}_{(a)}+\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}M_{t}}_{(b)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}}_{(a)}+\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}M_{t}}_{(b)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">We bound <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> via the usual elliptical potential lemma (<a href="#A7.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma G.3 (Elliptical Potential Lemma; Lemma 11 of ( ) ). ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}\leq 2d^{2}\log\left(1+\frac{\kappa T}{d^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}\leq 2d^{2}\log\left(1+\frac{\kappa T}{d^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">We now bound <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The crucial observation is that <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale difference sequence that satisfies <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{t\geq 1}|M_{t}|\leq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{t\geq 1}|M_{t}|\leq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, which prompts us to use the following variant of Freedman’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib98" title="" class="ltx_ref">Freedman, 1975</a>; <a href="#bib.bib113" title="" class="ltx_ref">Beygelzimer et al., 2011</a>)</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma 3 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al. (2024b)</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be a martingale difference sequence that satisfies <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{t\geq 1}|M_{t}|\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{t\geq 1}|M_{t}|\leq R</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in(0,1/R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in(0,1/R]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{s=1}^{t}M_{s}\leq(e-2)\xi\sum_{s=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}_{s-1}[M_{s}^{2}]+\frac{1}{\xi}\log\frac{2}{\delta},\quad\forall t\geq 1\right)\geq 1-\frac{\delta}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ξ</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{s=1}^{t}M_{s}\leq(e-2)\xi\sum_{s=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}_{s-1}[M_{s}^{2}]+\frac{1}{\xi}\log\frac{2}{\delta},\quad\forall t\geq 1\right)\geq 1-\frac{\delta}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">We will now show, with high probability, that the variance term induces a linear self-bounding inequality.
Denoting <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}Z_{s}}:={\bm{v}}_{s}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{s}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">Z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}Z_{s}}:={\bm{v}}_{s}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{s}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, which satisfies <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}Z_{s}}\leq\kappa\wedge 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">Z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">s</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}Z_{s}}\leq\kappa\wedge 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s-1}[M_{s}^{2}]\leq\mathbb{E}_{s-1}[{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}Z_{s}}^{2}]\leq(\kappa\wedge 1)\mathbb{E}_{s-1}[{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}Z_{s}}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mmultiscripts><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">Z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">s</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">Z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s-1}[M_{s}^{2}]\leq\mathbb{E}_{s-1}[{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}Z_{s}}^{2}]\leq(\kappa\wedge 1)\mathbb{E}_{s-1}[{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}Z_{s}}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p17.2" class="ltx_p">where the first inequality follows from the fact that for any random variable <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}[X]\leq\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}[X]\leq\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Choosing <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=\frac{\kappa\wedge 1}{2(e-2)}\leq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=\frac{\kappa\wedge 1}{2(e-2)}\leq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (Lemma 3 of ( ) ). ‣ Part I. 𝒪̃⁢(𝜂⁢𝛽⁢(log𝑇)^2) Regret Bound. ‣ B.1 Main Proof ‣ Appendix B Proof of : Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, the following holds with probability at least <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{\delta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{\delta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)=\sum_{t=1}^{T}M_{t}\leq\frac{(\kappa\wedge 1)^{2}}{2}\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{t-1}[{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}Z_{t}}]}_{={\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}\text{!}}+\frac{2(e-2)}{\kappa\wedge 1}\log\frac{2}{\delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">Z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>!</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)=\sum_{t=1}^{T}M_{t}\leq\frac{(\kappa\wedge 1)^{2}}{2}\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{t-1}[{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}Z_{t}}]}_{={\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}\text{!}}+\frac{2(e-2)}{\kappa\wedge 1}\log\frac{2}{\delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p19.1" class="ltx_p">Now bringing everything together for Eqn. (<a href="#A2.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Part I. 𝒪̃⁢(𝜂⁢𝛽⁢(log𝑇)^2) Regret Bound. ‣ B.1 Main Proof ‣ Appendix B Proof of : Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), the following holds with probability at least <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{\delta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{\delta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}=(a)+(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}=(a)+(b)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{2d^{2}\log\left(1+\frac{\kappa T}{d^{2}}\right)}_{(a)\leq}+\underbrace{\frac{(\kappa\wedge 1)^{2}}{2}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}+\frac{2(e-2)}{\kappa\wedge 1}\log\frac{2}{\delta}}_{(b)\leq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{2d^{2}\log\left(1+\frac{\kappa T}{d^{2}}\right)}_{(a)\leq}+\underbrace{\frac{(\kappa\wedge 1)^{2}}{2}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}+\frac{2(e-2)}{\kappa\wedge 1}\log\frac{2}{\delta}}_{(b)\leq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}+2d^{2}\log\left(1+\frac{\kappa T}{d^{2}}\right)+\frac{2(e-2)}{\kappa\wedge 1}\log\frac{2}{\delta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}+2d^{2}\log\left(1+\frac{\kappa T}{d^{2}}\right)+\frac{2(e-2)}{\kappa\wedge 1}\log\frac{2}{\delta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p19.2" class="ltx_p">which is a <em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p19.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008080;">linear, self-bounding inequality</em>!</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p20.1" class="ltx_p">Solving for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that with probability at least <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{\delta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{\delta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}\right]\leq 4d^{2}\log\left(1+\frac{\kappa T}{d^{2}}\right)+\frac{4(e-2)}{\kappa\wedge 1}\log\frac{2}{\delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF8040;" mathcolor="#BF8040">T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0.5,0.25}S_{T}}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[{\bm{v}}_{t}^{\top}{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}{\bm{v}}_{t}\right]\leq 4d^{2}\log\left(1+\frac{\kappa T}{d^{2}}\right)+\frac{4(e-2)}{\kappa\wedge 1}\log\frac{2}{\delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Combining everything at Eqn. (<a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Part I. 𝒪̃⁢(𝜂⁢𝛽⁢(log𝑇)^2) Regret Bound. ‣ B.1 Main Proof ‣ Appendix B Proof of : Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), we have that with probability at least <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> (after union bound with the confidence sequence),</p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)\lesssim{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta\kappa^{-1}d^{2}C_{\min}^{-1}\left(\log\frac{T}{d}\right)\left(d^{2}\log\frac{\kappa T}{d}+\kappa^{-1}\log\frac{1}{\delta}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)\lesssim{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta\kappa^{-1}d^{2}C_{\min}^{-1}\left(\log\frac{T}{d}\right)\left(d^{2}\log\frac{\kappa T}{d}+\kappa^{-1}\log\frac{1}{\delta}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part II. <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}(\sqrt{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}(\sqrt{T})</annotation></semantics></math> Regret Bound.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>-independent bound of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3 A New Analysis of Regularized Regret ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we get</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{L_{\mu}}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}+\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{L_{\mu}}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}+\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{L_{\mu}}{2}\sqrt{T\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]}+\frac{L_{\mu}}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{L_{\mu}}{2}\sqrt{T\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]}+\frac{L_{\mu}}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Cauchy-Schwarz &amp; Jensen)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{T\kappa^{-1}d^{4}C_{\min}^{-1}\left(\log\frac{T}{d}\right)^{2}}+\kappa^{-1}d^{4}C_{\min}^{-1}\left(\log\frac{T}{d}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{T\kappa^{-1}d^{4}C_{\min}^{-1}\left(\log\frac{T}{d}\right)^{2}}+\kappa^{-1}d^{4}C_{\min}^{-1}\left(\log\frac{T}{d}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Part I)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\kappa^{-\frac{1}{2}}C_{\min}^{-\frac{1}{2}}d^{2}\sqrt{T}\log\frac{T}{d}+\kappa^{-1}C_{\min}^{-1}d^{4}\left(\log\frac{T}{d}\right)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\kappa^{-\frac{1}{2}}C_{\min}^{-\frac{1}{2}}d^{2}\sqrt{T}\log\frac{T}{d}+\kappa^{-1}C_{\min}^{-1}d^{4}\left(\log\frac{T}{d}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2 (Coverage Lemma). ‣ Part I. 𝒪̃⁢(𝜂⁢𝛽⁢(log𝑇)^2) Regret Bound. ‣ B.1 Main Proof ‣ Appendix B Proof of : Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>: Coverage Lemma</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with this simple yet effective matrix lemma that will be useful throughout (we provide its proof at <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Proof of : PSD Matrix Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof of : Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> for completeness):</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\succeq{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\succeq{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{B}}\succeq{\bm{C}}\succeq{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{B}}\succeq{\bm{C}}\succeq{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> of compatible sizes, then <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}\succeq{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}\succeq{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{B}})\geq\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{B}})\geq\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin from the expectation on the RHS and work our way to the LHS:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\tr\left((\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\tr\left((\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex61.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\tr\left({\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})^{\top}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\tr\left({\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})^{\top}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Cyclic property of <math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tr\left({\bm{M}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})^{\top}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tr\left({\bm{M}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})^{\top}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Linearity of expectation)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex63.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tr\left({\bm{M}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tr\left({\bm{M}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Mixed-product property of <math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Now, let us examine <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Due to the linearity of the expectation and our assumption, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]=\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]\succeq C_{\min}\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes{\bm{I}}_{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]=\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]\succeq C_{\min}\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes{\bm{I}}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the last Lowener order follows from <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.2 Proof of : Coverage Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof of : Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>.
Then, again by <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.2 Proof of : Coverage Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof of : Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we have that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes\tilde{\bm{\phi}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tr\left({\bm{M}}\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tr\left({\bm{M}}\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\sim\rho}\left[\tilde{\bm{\phi}}\tilde{\bm{\phi}}^{\top}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq C_{\min}\tr\left({\bm{M}}\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes{\bm{I}}_{d}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq C_{\min}\tr\left({\bm{M}}\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes{\bm{I}}_{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{\min}\tr\left({\bm{M}}\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\left(\sum_{j=1}^{d}{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{\min}\tr\left({\bm{M}}\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes\left(\sum_{j=1}^{d}{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{\min}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\tr\left({\bm{M}}\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{\min}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\tr\left({\bm{M}}\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{\min}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\tr\left({\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{\min}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\tr\left({\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Mixed-product property of <math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{\min}\sum_{j=1}^{d}(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})^{\top}{\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{\min}\sum_{j=1}^{d}(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j})^{\top}{\bm{M}}(\bm{\phi}\otimes{\bm{e}}_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.2 Proof of : Coverage Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof of : Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>: PSD Matrix Lemma</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{D}}:={\bm{B}}-{\bm{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{D}}:={\bm{B}}-{\bm{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{B}}\succeq{\bm{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{B}}\succeq{\bm{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{D}}\succeq{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{D}}\succeq{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first show that <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}\succeq{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}\succeq{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By bilinearity of the Kronecker product,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}-{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{C}}={\bm{A}}\otimes({\bm{B}}-{\bm{C}})={\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{D}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}-{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{C}}={\bm{A}}\otimes({\bm{B}}-{\bm{C}})={\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{D}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">It therefore suffices to prove that <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\lambda_{i}({\bm{A}})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\lambda_{i}({\bm{A}})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\lambda_{j}({\bm{D}})\}_{j=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\lambda_{j}({\bm{D}})\}_{j=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the eigenvalues of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. A standard property of Kronecker products implies that the eigenvalues of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="A2.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\{\lambda_{i}({\bm{A}})\lambda_{j}({\bm{D}})\bigr\}_{i\in[n],\,j\in[m]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{\lambda_{i}({\bm{A}})\lambda_{j}({\bm{D}})\bigr\}_{i\in[n],\,j\in[m]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\succeq{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\succeq{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{D}}\succeq{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{D}}\succeq{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, all eigenvalues <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}({\bm{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}({\bm{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{j}({\bm{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{j}({\bm{D}})</annotation></semantics></math> are nonnegative, hence so are all products <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}({\bm{A}})\lambda_{j}({\bm{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}({\bm{A}})\lambda_{j}({\bm{D}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{D}}\succeq{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{D}}\succeq{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}\succeq{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}\succeq{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we prove <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{B}})\geq\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{B}})\geq\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a symmetric square root <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}={\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}={\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using cyclicity of trace,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{D}})=\tr({\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}})=\tr({\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}}{\bm{A}}^{1/2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{D}})=\tr({\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}})=\tr({\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Moreover, <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite. For any <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,
letting <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}:={\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}:={\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{x}}={\bm{y}}^{\top}{\bm{D}}{\bm{y}}\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{x}}={\bm{y}}^{\top}{\bm{D}}{\bm{y}}\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where the inequality uses <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{D}}\succeq{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{D}}\succeq{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}\succeq{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}}{\bm{A}}^{1/2}\succeq{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore
<math id="A2.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr({\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}}{\bm{A}}^{1/2})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr({\bm{A}}^{1/2}{\bm{D}}{\bm{A}}^{1/2})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{D}})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr({\bm{A}}{\bm{D}})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Coverage Lemma without Feature Diversity</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we show that for specific choices of <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2 (Coverage Lemma). ‣ Part I. 𝒪̃⁢(𝜂⁢𝛽⁢(log𝑇)^2) Regret Bound. ‣ B.1 Main Proof ‣ Appendix B Proof of : Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> holds <span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">even without the feature diversity assumption (<a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Feature Map and Diversity). ‣ Feature Diversity. ‣ 2.1 (Self-Play) Interaction Protocol ‣ 2 Problem Setting ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)</span>, where <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\min}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\min}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced with a function of <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Recalling that <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi=\Delta({\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi=\Delta({\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Coverage Lemma without Feature Diversity)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> be a fixed policy, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the corresponding regularized SNE policy with respect to the preference model <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}_{t}:=\argmax_{\pi^{1}\in\Pi}\min_{\pi^{2}\in\Pi}J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\pi^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}_{t}:=\argmax_{\pi^{1}\in\Pi}\min_{\pi^{2}\in\Pi}J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\pi^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Using the shorthand notation <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi({\bm{a}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi({\bm{a}})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi({\bm{x}},{\bm{a}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi({\bm{x}},{\bm{a}})</annotation></semantics></math>, for any positive semi-definite matrix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}\succeq{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}\succeq{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{a}}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})\right]\leq{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}h(\eta)}\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{a}}\sim\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}}\left[\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{a}}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})\right]\leq{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}h(\eta)}\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{a}}\sim\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}}\left[\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}h(\eta)}=\begin{cases}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{\eta}},&amp;$\psi(\cdot)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})$,\\
{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta},&amp;$\psi(\cdot)=D_{\chi^{2}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})$,\\
{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}1+\eta},&amp;$\psi(\cdot)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+D_{\chi^{2}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})$.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">e</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">,</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">,</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">.</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}h(\eta)}=\begin{cases}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{\eta}},&amp;$\psi(\cdot)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})$,\\
{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta},&amp;$\psi(\cdot)=D_{\chi^{2}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})$,\\
{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}1+\eta},&amp;$\psi(\cdot)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+D_{\chi^{2}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})$.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We present the proof for a finite action space <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The results naturally extend to infinite <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> via integration.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can bound the left-hand side by expanding the expectation and applying a density ratio bound:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{a}}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{a}}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}\right)\sum_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}\right)\sum_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}\right)\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{a}}\sim\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}}\left[\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}\right)\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{a}}\sim\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}}\left[\phi({\bm{a}})^{\top}{\bm{M}}\phi({\bm{a}})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, it remains to bound the maximum density ratio between the regularized optimal policy <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the reference policy <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case I. <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\cdot)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\cdot)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A2.SS4.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a, Proposition 3)</a></cite>, we have:</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})=\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})\exp({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}},\hat{\pi}_{t}))}{\sum_{{\bm{a}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}}^{\prime})\exp({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}}^{\prime},\hat{\pi}_{t}))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})=\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})\exp({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}},\hat{\pi}_{t}))}{\sum_{{\bm{a}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}}^{\prime})\exp({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}}^{\prime},\hat{\pi}_{t}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since preference probabilities satisfy <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{t}(\cdot,\cdot)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{t}(\cdot,\cdot)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\in\Delta({\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\in\Delta({\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{{\bm{a}}^{\prime}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}}^{\prime})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{{\bm{a}}^{\prime}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}}^{\prime})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}=\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\exp({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}},\hat{\pi}_{t}))}{\sum_{{\bm{a}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}}^{\prime})\exp({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}}^{\prime},\hat{\pi}_{t}))}\leq\frac{\exp({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta})}{\sum_{{\bm{a}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}}^{\prime})}={\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{\eta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">e</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}=\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\exp({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}},\hat{\pi}_{t}))}{\sum_{{\bm{a}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}}^{\prime})\exp({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}}^{\prime},\hat{\pi}_{t}))}\leq\frac{\exp({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta})}{\sum_{{\bm{a}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}}^{\prime})}={\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{\eta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case II. <math id="A2.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\cdot)=D_{\chi^{2}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\cdot)=D_{\chi^{2}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A2.SS4.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We directly invoke <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib126" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. (2025a, Eqn. (10))</a></cite>, which states that under chi-squared regularization,</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}=\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\max\left\{{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\left(\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}},\hat{\pi}_{t})-Z\right),0\right\}\leq{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}=\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\max\left\{{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\left(\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}},\hat{\pi}_{t})-Z\right),0\right\}\leq{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is an appropriate normalization constant and we again utilize the fact that <math id="A2.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{t}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{t}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case III. <math id="A2.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\cdot)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+D_{\chi^{2}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\cdot)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+D_{\chi^{2}}(\cdot,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A2.SS4.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We directly invoke <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib127" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. (2025b, Proposition 4.1)</a></cite>, which states that under mixed chi-squared regularization,</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}\leq 1+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{{\bm{a}}\in{\mathcal{A}}}\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}\leq 1+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Towards General <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-Divergence)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note that all three regularizers above are specific instances of the <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib131" title="" class="ltx_ref">Csiszár, 1963</a>; <a href="#bib.bib132" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ali and Silvey, 1966</a>)</cite>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib136" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2024, Theorem 1)</a></cite> proved that if <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\not\in\mathrm{dom}(f^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>dom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\not\in\mathrm{dom}(f^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, then in our general preference scenario, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}=(f^{\prime})^{-1}\left({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\left(\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}},\hat{\pi}_{t})-Z\right)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\hat{\pi}_{t}({\bm{a}})}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{a}})}=(f^{\prime})^{-1}\left({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\left(\hat{P}_{t}({\bm{a}},\hat{\pi}_{t})-Z\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is an appropriate normalization constant.
Thus, we postulate that a similar coverage lemma can be proven for various other choices of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, completely bypassing the feature diversity assumption.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5.1 Nuclear-Norm Regularized MLE and Regret Bound ‣ 5 poly(𝑑)-free 𝒪̃⁢(√𝜂⁢𝑇∧𝑇^{2/3}) via ETC ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>: Regret Bound of Explore-Then-Commit</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Main Proof</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the nuclear-norm regularized MLE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib108" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fan et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2025</a>)</cite>: denoting <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}_{t}:=\phi({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}_{t}^{1})\phi({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}_{t}^{2})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}_{t}:=\phi({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}_{t}^{1})\phi({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}_{t}^{2})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{T_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{T_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leftarrow\argmin_{\bm{\Theta}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d)}{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta})+\lambda_{T_{0}}\left\lVert\bm{\Theta}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>nuc</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leftarrow\argmin_{\bm{\Theta}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d)}{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta})+\lambda_{T_{0}}\left\lVert\bm{\Theta}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\frac{1}{T_{0}}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\left\{m(\langle\bm{\Theta},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle)-r_{t}\langle\bm{\Theta},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\frac{1}{T_{0}}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\left\{m(\langle\bm{\Theta},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle)-r_{t}\langle\bm{\Theta},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We also introduce the following assumption used commonly in logistic and generalized linear bandits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abeille et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Russac et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The link function <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">self-concordant with constant <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{s}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{s}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\ddot{\mu}\left(\bm{\phi}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}\bm{\phi}^{\prime}\right)\right|\leq R_{s}\dot{\mu}\left(\bm{\phi}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}\bm{\phi}^{\prime}\right),\quad\forall\bm{\phi},\bm{\phi}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(1),\forall\bm{\Theta}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\ddot{\mu}\left(\bm{\phi}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}\bm{\phi}^{\prime}\right)\right|\leq R_{s}\dot{\mu}\left(\bm{\phi}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}\bm{\phi}^{\prime}\right),\quad\forall\bm{\phi},\bm{\phi}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(1),\forall\bm{\Theta}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Lastly, we define the following instance-specific curvature quantity:</p>
<table id="A3.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\star}:=\min_{\bm{\phi},\bm{\phi}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{B}^{d}(1)}\dot{\mu}\left(\bm{\phi}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{\star}\bm{\phi}^{\prime}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\star}:=\min_{\bm{\phi},\bm{\phi}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{B}^{d}(1)}\dot{\mu}\left(\bm{\phi}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{\star}\bm{\phi}^{\prime}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This parameter has been identified as a fundamental instance-dependent factor in the analysis of logistic and generalized linear bandits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abeille et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>.
In contrast to the global curvature <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> (see <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 2.2 (Generalized Bilinear Preference Model). ‣ 2.2 Generalized Bilinear Preference Model (GBPM) ‣ 2 Problem Setting ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>), which involves an additional minimization over <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}_{\star}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}_{\star}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> captures the local geometry around the true parameter <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We note that in many practical regimes, the global bound may be overly pessimistic, such that <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}\gg\kappa_{\star}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≫</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}\gg\kappa_{\star}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this Appendix, we show that under the additional assumption that <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is self-concordant, we can obtain dependencies w.r.t. <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\star}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\star}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma provides a Frobenius error guarantee for the nuclear-norm regularized MLE <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="124.15" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 124.15" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,124.15) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 118.24 C 0 121.5 2.64 124.15 5.91 124.15 L 471.47 124.15 C 474.73 124.15 477.38 121.5 477.38 118.24 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 118.24 C 1.97 120.42 3.73 122.18 5.91 122.18 L 471.47 122.18 C 473.65 122.18 475.41 120.42 475.41 118.24 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 100.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:6.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="96.59" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\kappa}\in\{\kappa,\kappa_{\star}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\kappa}\in\{\kappa,\kappa_{\star}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is such that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\kappa}=\kappa_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\kappa}=\kappa_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> if <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ C.1 Main Proof ‣ Appendix C Proof of : Regret Bound of Explore-Then-Commit ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> holds, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\kappa}=\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\kappa}=\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> if otherwise.
Suppose that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.5,0,0.5}T_{0}\gtrsim\tilde{\kappa}^{-2}C_{\min}^{-4}dr\log\frac{d}{\delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">≳</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">C</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">min</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">4</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.5,0,0.5}T_{0}\gtrsim\tilde{\kappa}^{-2}C_{\min}^{-4}dr\log\frac{d}{\delta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{T_{0}}=\sqrt{\frac{32L_{\mu}\log\frac{4d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{T_{0}}=\sqrt{\frac{32L_{\mu}\log\frac{4d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\left\lVert\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}-\bm{\Theta}_{\star}\right\rVert_{F}\lesssim\frac{1}{\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{L_{\mu}r\log\frac{d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}\right)\geq 1-\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚯</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚯</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">‖</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≲</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\left\lVert\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}-\bm{\Theta}_{\star}\right\rVert_{F}\lesssim\frac{1}{\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{L_{\mu}r\log\frac{d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}\right)\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof largely follows the classical M-estimator analysis via restricted strong convexity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib109" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wainwright, 2019</a>)</cite>, which we reproduce here for completeness.
See <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Proof of : Error Bound Guarantee of the Nuclear-Norm Regularized MLE ‣ Appendix C Proof of : Regret Bound of Explore-Then-Commit ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> for the full proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We first invoke the <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent bound of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3 A New Analysis of Regularized Regret ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and the above lemma to <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[[T_{0}+1,T]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[[T_{0}+1,T]]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)\lesssim T_{0}+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta\sum_{t=T_{0}+1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]\leq T_{0}+T{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{T_{0}}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\lesssim T_{0}+\frac{T{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta}{\tilde{\kappa}^{2}C_{\min}^{4}}\frac{r\log\frac{d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)\lesssim T_{0}+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta\sum_{t=T_{0}+1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]\leq T_{0}+T{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{T_{0}}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\lesssim T_{0}+\frac{T{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}\beta}{\tilde{\kappa}^{2}C_{\min}^{4}}\frac{r\log\frac{d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">This balances out when <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}\asymp\tilde{\kappa}^{-1}C_{\min}^{-2}\sqrt{T\eta\beta r\log\frac{d}{\delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≍</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}\asymp\tilde{\kappa}^{-1}C_{\min}^{-2}\sqrt{T\eta\beta r\log\frac{d}{\delta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we invoke the <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>-independent bound of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3 A New Analysis of Regularized Regret ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, which yields</p>
<table id="A3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim T_{0}+\sum_{t=T_{0}+1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}\right]+\sum_{t=T_{0}+1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim T_{0}+\sum_{t=T_{0}+1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}\right]+\sum_{t=T_{0}+1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}_{t}\sim\hat{\pi}_{t}}\left[\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{t}\bm{\phi}_{t}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq T_{0}+T\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{T_{0}}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}+T\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{T_{0}}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq T_{0}+T\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{T_{0}}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}+T\left\lVert{\bm{E}}_{T_{0}}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim T_{0}+\frac{T}{\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{L_{\mu}r\log\frac{d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}+\frac{T}{\tilde{\kappa}^{2}C_{\min}^{4}}\frac{L_{\mu}r\log\frac{d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim T_{0}+\frac{T}{\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{L_{\mu}r\log\frac{d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}+\frac{T}{\tilde{\kappa}^{2}C_{\min}^{4}}\frac{L_{\mu}r\log\frac{d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">This balances out when <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}\asymp\left(T^{2}\tilde{\kappa}^{-2}C_{\min}^{-4}r\log\frac{d}{\delta}\right)^{1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≍</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}\asymp\left(T^{2}\tilde{\kappa}^{-2}C_{\min}^{-4}r\log\frac{d}{\delta}\right)^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\gtrsim\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}r\log\frac{d}{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≳</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\gtrsim\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}r\log\frac{d}{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the latter which we can assume to hold without loss of any generality.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ C.1 Main Proof ‣ Appendix C Proof of : Regret Bound of Explore-Then-Commit ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>: Error Bound Guarantee of the Nuclear-Norm Regularized MLE</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the usual recipe for proving the error rate of a generic M-estimator with a convex regularizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib109" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wainwright, 2019</a>, Chapter 9 &amp; 10)</cite>.
Let <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> be given.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that</p>
<table id="A3.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}:=\argmin_{\bm{\Theta}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d)}{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta})+\lambda_{T_{0}}\left\lVert\bm{\Theta}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}},\quad{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}):=\frac{1}{T_{0}}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\left\{m({\bm{x}}_{t}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}_{t})-r_{t}{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}_{t}\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>nuc</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}:=\argmin_{\bm{\Theta}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d)}{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta})+\lambda_{T_{0}}\left\lVert\bm{\Theta}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}},\quad{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}):=\frac{1}{T_{0}}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\left\{m({\bm{x}}_{t}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}_{t})-r_{t}{\bm{x}}_{t}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}_{t}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Recall that for notational simplicity, we denote <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}_{t}:=\bm{\phi}_{t}^{1}(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{2})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}_{t}:=\bm{\phi}_{t}^{1}(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{2})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We will collect all requirements on <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> in <span id="A3.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;">violet</span> to be aggregated at the end of the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The first lemma tells us the correct choice of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{T_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{T_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the gradient of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> at the true parameter <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is well bounded:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma C.3 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al. (2025)</a></cite>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;"> <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}\geq\frac{2}{9L_{\mu}}\log\frac{4d}{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">≥</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">2</mn><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">μ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">d</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}\geq\frac{2}{9L_{\mu}}\log\frac{4d}{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Then, choosing <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{T_{0}}=\sqrt{\frac{32L_{\mu}\log\frac{4d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{T_{0}}=\sqrt{\frac{32L_{\mu}\log\frac{4d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\left\lVert\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta})\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\frac{\lambda_{T_{0}}}{2}\right)\geq 1-\frac{\delta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\left\lVert\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta})\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\frac{\lambda_{T_{0}}}{2}\right)\geq 1-\frac{\delta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We will suppose that the above good event holds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We now recall the definition of restricted strong convexity (RSC):</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Definition 9.15 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib109" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wainwright (2019)</a></cite>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We say that <span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">restricted strong convexity (RSC)</span> with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\tau,R\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\tau,R\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> if</span></p>
<table id="A3.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+\Delta)-{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star})-\langle\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}),\Delta\rangle}_{\text{Bregman divergence generated by ${\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}$}}\geq\frac{\alpha}{2}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{F}^{2}-\tau^{2}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}}^{2},\quad\forall\Delta\in{\mathcal{B}}^{d}_{F}(R)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Bregman divergence generated by </mtext><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">ℒ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></msub></msub></mrow></munder><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>nuc</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+\Delta)-{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star})-\langle\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}),\Delta\rangle}_{\text{Bregman divergence generated by ${\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}$}}\geq\frac{\alpha}{2}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{F}^{2}-\tau^{2}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}}^{2},\quad\forall\Delta\in{\mathcal{B}}^{d}_{F}(R).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The next lemma shows that the above holds with high probability:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.4</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;"> <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}\gtrsim C_{\min}^{-4}\tilde{\kappa}^{-2}dr\log\frac{d}{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">≳</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">C</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">min</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">4</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}\gtrsim C_{\min}^{-4}\tilde{\kappa}^{-2}dr\log\frac{d}{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.
Then, with probability at least <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{\delta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{\delta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RSC</span> holds with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Lastly, noting that the subspace Lipschitz constant <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib109" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wainwright, 2019</a>, Definition 9.18)</cite> of <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>nuc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude by invoking the “master theorem” for nuclear-norm regularized estimator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib109" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wainwright, 2019</a>, Theorem 9.19)</cite>:</p>
<table id="A3.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\left\lVert\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}-\bm{\Theta}_{\star}\right\rVert_{F}\leq\frac{12}{\tilde{R}_{s}C_{\min}^{2}\tilde{\kappa}}\sqrt{\frac{2L_{\mu}r\log\frac{4d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}\right)\geq 1-\delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\left\lVert\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}-\bm{\Theta}_{\star}\right\rVert_{F}\leq\frac{12}{\tilde{R}_{s}C_{\min}^{2}\tilde{\kappa}}\sqrt{\frac{2L_{\mu}r\log\frac{4d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}\right)\geq 1-\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">given</em> that <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{12}{\tilde{R}_{s}C_{\min}^{2}\tilde{\kappa}}\sqrt{\frac{2L_{\mu}r\log\frac{4d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{12}{\tilde{R}_{s}C_{\min}^{2}\tilde{\kappa}}\sqrt{\frac{2L_{\mu}r\log\frac{4d}{\delta}}{T_{0}}}\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is true when <span id="A3.SS2.p7.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;"> <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}\gtrsim C_{\min}^{-4}\tilde{\kappa}^{-2}dr\log\frac{d}{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">≳</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">C</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">min</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">4</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}\gtrsim C_{\min}^{-4}\tilde{\kappa}^{-2}dr\log\frac{d}{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4. ‣ C.2 Proof of : Error Bound Guarantee of the Nuclear-Norm Regularized MLE ‣ Appendix C Proof of : Regret Bound of Explore-Then-Commit ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Taylor’s expansion with integral remainder, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+\Delta)-{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star})-\langle\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}),\Delta\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+\Delta)-{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star})-\langle\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}),\Delta\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T_{0}}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\left\{m(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle)-m(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle)-\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle m^{\prime}(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle)\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T_{0}}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\left\{m(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle)-m(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle)-\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle m^{\prime}(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T_{0}}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\langle\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle^{2}\int_{0}^{1}(1-z)\underbrace{m^{\prime\prime}\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+z\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right)}_{=\dot{\mu}\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+z\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right)}dz." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T_{0}}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\langle\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle^{2}\int_{0}^{1}(1-z)\underbrace{m^{\prime\prime}\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+z\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right)}_{=\dot{\mu}\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+z\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right)}dz.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now divide into two cases:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> is self-concordant.<span id="A3.SS2.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
If this is the case, then we can utilize the following self-concordance control lemma:</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma 9 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abeille et al. (2021)</a></cite>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>-self-concordant <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> that is monotone increasing, the following holds: for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},z_{2}\in{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},z_{2}\in{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mu}(z_{2})\exp(-R_{s}|z_{1}-z_{2}|)\leq\dot{\mu}(z_{1})\leq\dot{\mu}(z_{2})\exp(R_{s}|z_{1}-z_{2}|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mu}(z_{2})\exp(-R_{s}|z_{1}-z_{2}|)\leq\dot{\mu}(z_{1})\leq\dot{\mu}(z_{2})\exp(R_{s}|z_{1}-z_{2}|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We choose <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies that by Hölder’s inequality, <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\langle\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\langle\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, by the above self-concordance lemma,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}(1-z)\dot{\mu}\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+z\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right)dz\geq\int_{0}^{1}(1-z)e^{-R_{s}z}\dot{\mu}\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right)dz\geq\kappa_{\star}\tilde{R}_{s}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}(1-z)\dot{\mu}\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+z\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right)dz\geq\int_{0}^{1}(1-z)e^{-R_{s}z}\dot{\mu}\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star},{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right)dz\geq\kappa_{\star}\tilde{R}_{s},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we define the constant</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{s}:=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{2},&amp;\quad$R_{s}=0$\\
\frac{R_{s}-1+e^{-R_{s}}}{R_{s}^{2}},&amp;\quad$R_{s}&gt;0$.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext> </mtext><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext> </mtext><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{s}:=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{2},&amp;\quad$R_{s}=0$\\
\frac{R_{s}-1+e^{-R_{s}}}{R_{s}^{2}},&amp;\quad$R_{s}&gt;0$.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Otherwise.<span id="A3.SS2.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
If not, then we simply lower bound</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}(1-z)\dot{\mu}\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+z\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right)dz\geq\kappa\int_{0}^{1}(1-z)dz=\frac{\kappa}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}(1-z)\dot{\mu}\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+z\Delta,{\bm{X}}_{t}\rangle\right)dz\geq\kappa\int_{0}^{1}(1-z)dz=\frac{\kappa}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">With a slight overload of notation, if self-concordance does not hold, we define <math id="A3.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{s}=\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{s}=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Concluding the proof.<span id="A3.SS2.p13.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let us define the vectorized population and empirical design matrices:</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}:=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{X}}}\left[\mathrm{\mathrm{vec}}({\bm{X}})\mathrm{\mathrm{vec}}({\bm{X}})^{\top}\right],\quad\widehat{{\bm{V}}}:=\frac{1}{T_{0}}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\mathrm{vec}({\bm{X}}_{t})\mathrm{vec}({\bm{X}}_{t})^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝑿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}:=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{X}}}\left[\mathrm{\mathrm{vec}}({\bm{X}})\mathrm{\mathrm{vec}}({\bm{X}})^{\top}\right],\quad\widehat{{\bm{V}}}:=\frac{1}{T_{0}}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\mathrm{vec}({\bm{X}}_{t})\mathrm{vec}({\bm{X}}_{t})^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex97.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex97.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}^{1},\bm{\phi}^{2}}\left[(\bm{\phi}^{2}\otimes\bm{\phi}^{1})(\bm{\phi}^{2}\otimes\bm{\phi}^{1})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}^{1},\bm{\phi}^{2}}\left[(\bm{\phi}^{2}\otimes\bm{\phi}^{1})(\bm{\phi}^{2}\otimes\bm{\phi}^{1})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A3.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{vec}({\bm{a}}{\bm{b}}^{\top})={\bm{b}}\otimes{\bm{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{vec}({\bm{a}}{\bm{b}}^{\top})={\bm{b}}\otimes{\bm{a}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}^{1},\bm{\phi}^{2}}\left[(\bm{\phi}^{2}(\bm{\phi}^{2})^{\top})\otimes(\bm{\phi}^{1}(\bm{\phi}^{1})^{\top})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}^{1},\bm{\phi}^{2}}\left[(\bm{\phi}^{2}(\bm{\phi}^{2})^{\top})\otimes(\bm{\phi}^{1}(\bm{\phi}^{1})^{\top})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(mixed product property of the Kronecker product)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex99.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}}\left[\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\right]^{\otimes 2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}}\left[\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\right]^{\otimes 2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A3.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\phi}^{1}\overset{d}{=}\bm{\phi}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\phi}^{1}\overset{d}{=}\bm{\phi}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">and thus, <math id="A3.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}\left({\bm{V}}\right)=\lambda_{\min}\left(\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}}\left[\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\right]\right)^{2}\geq C_{\min}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}\left({\bm{V}}\right)=\lambda_{\min}\left(\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\phi}}\left[\bm{\phi}\bm{\phi}^{\top}\right]\right)^{2}\geq C_{\min}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Feature Map and Diversity). ‣ Feature Diversity. ‣ 2.1 (Self-Play) Interaction Protocol ‣ 2 Problem Setting ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+\Delta)-{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star})-\langle\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}),\Delta\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}+\Delta)-{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star})-\langle\nabla{\mathcal{L}}_{T_{0}}(\bm{\Theta}_{\star}),\Delta\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex100.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)^{\top}\widehat{{\bm{V}}}\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)^{\top}\widehat{{\bm{V}}}\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)^{\top}{\bm{V}}\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)+\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)^{\top}(\widehat{{\bm{V}}}-{\bm{V}})\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)^{\top}{\bm{V}}\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)+\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)^{\top}(\widehat{{\bm{V}}}-{\bm{V}})\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{F}^{2}-\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}\underbrace{\left|\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)^{\top}(\widehat{{\bm{V}}}-{\bm{V}})\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)\right|}_{\triangleq{\mathcal{E}}_{T_{0}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{F}^{2}-\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}\underbrace{\left|\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)^{\top}(\widehat{{\bm{V}}}-{\bm{V}})\mathrm{vec}(\Delta)\right|}_{\triangleq{\mathcal{E}}_{T_{0}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the standard empirical process theory and peeling argument over the ball <math id="A3.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}_{F}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}_{F}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> (see, e.g., proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib109" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wainwright (2019, Theorem 10.17)</a></cite>), one can establish that the deviation is uniformly bounded as</span></p>
<table id="A3.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left({\mathcal{E}}_{T_{0}}\leq\frac{\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}}{2}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{F}^{2}\right)\geq 1-\frac{\delta}{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left({\mathcal{E}}_{T_{0}}\leq\frac{\tilde{R}_{s}\tilde{\kappa}C_{\min}^{2}}{2}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{F}^{2}\right)\geq 1-\frac{\delta}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">provided <span id="A3.SS2.p16.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;"> <math id="A3.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}\gtrsim C_{\min}^{-4}\tilde{\kappa}^{-2}dr\log\frac{d}{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">≳</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">C</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">min</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">4</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#800080;" mathcolor="#800080">δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}\gtrsim C_{\min}^{-4}\tilde{\kappa}^{-2}dr\log\frac{d}{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Discussions on Regrets</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Four Regret Definitions and Discussions</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A standard measure of performance in online learning is <em id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">regret</em>. However, because the interaction is two-player and self-play, there are several ways to define regret, arising from different yet closely related communities: no-regret learning in games, dueling bandits/RL, and RL in two-player zero-sum games.
In the main text, we consider only two regrets (<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ABR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ABR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ABR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>) for brevity, and so in this Appendix, we provide the deferred discussions regarding four regrets:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="321.43" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 321.43" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,321.43) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 315.52 C 0 318.78 2.64 321.43 5.91 321.43 L 471.47 321.43 C 474.73 321.43 477.38 318.78 477.38 315.52 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 315.52 C 1.97 317.7 3.73 319.46 5.91 319.46 L 471.47 319.46 C 473.65 319.46 475.41 317.7 475.41 315.52 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 298.04)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:20.54em;font-size:10pt;" height="293.87" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The four regrets are defined as follows.</span></span>
<span id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A4.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<span id="A4.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Average-Nash Regret</span><span id="A4.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A4.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AN\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T):=\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}\in\Pi}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}},\pi^{2})\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">AN</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AN\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T):=\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}\in\Pi}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}},\pi^{2})\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<span id="A4.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Average-Best-Response Regret</span><span id="A4.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A4.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ABR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T):=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}\in\Pi}\left\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}},\pi^{2})\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ABR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ABR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T):=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}\in\Pi}\left\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}},\pi^{2})\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<span id="A4.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Max-Nash Regret</span><span id="A4.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A4.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MN\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T):=\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\{\frac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}},\pi)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">MN</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MN\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T):=\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\{\frac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}},\pi)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<span id="A4.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Max-Best-Response Regret</span><span id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A4.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T):=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left\{\frac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}},\pi)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T):=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left\{\frac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}},\pi)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The unregularized variants are defined similarly and denoted without the <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> subscript.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Categorization Criteria.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There are two criteria that determine each regret definition.
The first criterion is, at each time <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, whether to consider the regrets of both players simultaneously, or to consider the regret of the max-player only.
This distinguishes between <em id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Average</em> or <em id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Max</em>.
The second criterion is whether to compare against a fixed comparator or to compare against the best response at each time <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, which is usually time-varying.
This distinguishes between <em id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Nash</em> and <em id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Best-Response</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, the <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Average</span> regret definitions consider the “suboptimality” of both policies simultaneously. The difference between <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Nash</span> and <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Best-Response</span> is whether the regret is defined w.r.t. a fixed comparator (<span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Nash</span>) or a dynamically changing comparator (<span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Best-Response</span>).
Thus, in classical literature, they are also known as <em id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">external</em> and <em id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">internal (swap)</em> regrets.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Average Regrets.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AN\text{-}Reg}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>AN</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AN\text{-}Reg}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> is the notion originally considered in the seminal work of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Freund and Schapire (1999)</a></cite>, followed by numerous works on no-regret learning dynamics in games <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib75" title="" class="ltx_ref">Daskalakis et al., 2011</a>; <a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Daskalakis et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Daskalakis et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rakhlin and Sridharan, 2013a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rakhlin and Sridharan, 2013b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Syrgkanis et al., 2015</a>)</cite>, recently adopted to game-theoretic LLM alignment <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025c</a>)</cite>.
<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AN\text{-}Reg}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>AN</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AN\text{-}Reg}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely the regret considered in contextual dueling bandits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dudík et al., 2015</a>, Eqn. (3))</cite> and dueling RL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Saha et al., 2023</a>, Eqn. (4))</cite>; indeed, for any <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>, utilizing the anti-symmetry of <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can rewrite
<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi,{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}})-J({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}},\pi)=J(\pi,{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}})+J(\pi,{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}})-1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi,{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}})-J({\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}},\pi)=J(\pi,{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1}})+J(\pi,{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}})-1.</annotation></semantics></math>
This also slightly resembles Borda regret in dueling bandits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Saha et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and average regret in dueling bandits under linear stochastic transitivity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Saha, 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bengs et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bengs et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ABR\text{-}Reg}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ABR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ABR\text{-}Reg}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> strongly resembles the notion of <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">best response regret</span> in adversarial dueling bandits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Saha and Krishnamurthy, 2022</a>, Eqn. (1))</cite>, but there is a key difference.
In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Saha and Krishnamurthy (2022)</a></cite>, the comparator at time <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the same for both players, whereas in our regret setting, it differs for each player.
Basically, each player must compete with the worst-case (strongest) adversary from her perspective, who chooses the best response from his perspective.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Max Regrets.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The notion of considering the regret of the <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">max</span> player dates back to the self-play framework for RL in two-player zero-sum games <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai and Jin, 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al., 2022</a>)</cite>; this idea has been recently applied to theoretical analyses of online RLHF under general preference <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>.
Basically, the intuition is that the learner only cares about obtaining the NE policy for the max-player, which is the policy that is actually deployed in practice.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the min-player’s policies <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> do not contribute to the regret at all, and thus, often, the min-player acts as an exploration agent whose sole role is to collect as much information as possible to facilitate the learning of the max-player <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai and Jin, 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Online-to-Batch Conversion</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A standard consequence of no-regret learning in repeated zero-sum games is an <em id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">online-to-batch conversion</em>: the time-averaged (mixed) policies form an approximate Nash equilibrium. We formalize this statement in the following proposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Online-to-batch conversion)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2})\}_{t=1}^{T}\subseteq\Pi\times\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2})\}_{t=1}^{T}\subseteq\Pi\times\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> be any policy sequence.
Define the uniform mixture policies as <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\pi}_{T}^{i}:=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\pi}_{T}^{i}:=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\hat{\pi}_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> and for simplicity, let us denote <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\pi}_{T}:=\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\pi}_{T}:=\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(a) Average regrets.</span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For average regrets, </span><math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1},\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1},\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a </span><math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{Reg}(T)}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>Reg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{Reg}(T)}{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-approximate symmetric NE:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}\in\Pi}\Bigl\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1},\pi^{2})\Bigr\}\;\leq\;\frac{\mathrm{AN\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)}{T}\;\leq\;\frac{\mathrm{ABR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)}{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>AN</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ABR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}\in\Pi}\Bigl\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1},\pi^{2})\Bigr\}\;\leq\;\frac{\mathrm{AN\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)}{T}\;\leq\;\frac{\mathrm{ABR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)}{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(b) Max regrets.</span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For max regrets, </span><math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\pi}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\pi}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a </span><math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2\mathrm{Reg}(T)}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2\mathrm{Reg}(T)}{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-approximate symmetric NE:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\Bigl\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi,\bar{\pi}_{T})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T},\pi)\Bigr\}\;\leq\;\frac{2\mathrm{MN\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)}{T}\;\leq\;\frac{2\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)}{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\Bigl\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi,\bar{\pi}_{T})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T},\pi)\Bigr\}\;\leq\;\frac{2\mathrm{MN\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)}{T}\;\leq\;\frac{2\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)}{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(a)<span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Fix any <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{1},\pi^{2}\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{1},\pi^{2}\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the bilinearity of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> and Jensen’s inequality w.r.t. <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})=J(\pi^{1},\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}\psi(\pi^{1})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}\psi(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})\leq\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})=J(\pi^{1},\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}\psi(\pi^{1})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}\psi(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})\leq\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and similarly,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1},\pi^{2})=J(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1},\pi^{2})-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}\psi(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}\psi(\pi^{2})\geq\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1},\pi^{2})=J(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1},\pi^{2})-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}\psi(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}\psi(\pi^{2})\geq\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting the two inequalities and taking <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}}\Bigl\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1},\pi^{2})\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}}\Bigl\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\bar{\pi}_{T}^{2})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T}^{1},\pi^{2})\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex111.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{T}\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Bigl(J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi^{2})\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{T}\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Bigl(J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi^{2})\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}}\Bigl(J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi^{2})\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi^{1},\pi^{2}}\Bigl(J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi^{1},\hat{\pi}_{t}^{2})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi^{2})\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(b)<span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> By the same averaging argument (bilinearity of <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> and Jensen’s inequality),
for every <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi,\bar{\pi}_{T})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T},\pi)\leq\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Bigl(J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi,\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi,\bar{\pi}_{T})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T},\pi)\leq\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Bigl(J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi,\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since for each <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi,\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)=2\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi,\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)=2\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>,
taking <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and substituting yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\bigl\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi,\bar{\pi}_{T})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T},\pi)\bigr\}\leq\frac{2}{T}\max_{\pi}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\Bigr)\leq\frac{2}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi}\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\Bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>π</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\bigl\{J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\pi,\bar{\pi}_{T})-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\bar{\pi}_{T},\pi)\bigr\}\leq\frac{2}{T}\max_{\pi}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\Bigr)\leq\frac{2}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi}\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Eluder Dimension of GBPM</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Upper Bounding the Eluder Dimension of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a)</a></cite></h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To instantiate the regret bound of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a)</a></cite> in <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Instantiating Regret Bound of ( ) to GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>, we first recall their specific notion of the eluder dimension:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Eluder dimension, General Preference Model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the general preference model, for any <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{t-1}=\{({\bm{x}}_{i},{\bm{a}}^{1}_{i},{\bm{a}}^{2}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{t-1}=\{({\bm{x}}_{i},{\bm{a}}^{1}_{i},{\bm{a}}^{2}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the uncertainty of <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\texttt{GP}}(\lambda,{\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2};\mathcal{P},\mathcal{D}_{t-1})=\sup_{P_{1},P_{2}\in\mathcal{P}}\frac{|P_{1}({\bm{a}}^{1}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}\mid{\bm{x}})-P_{2}({\bm{a}}^{1}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}\mid{\bm{x}})|}{\sqrt{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{1}({\bm{a}}^{1}_{s}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}_{s}\mid{\bm{x}}_{s})-P_{2}({\bm{a}}^{1}_{s}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}_{s}\mid{\bm{x}}_{s}))^{2}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\texttt{GP}}(\lambda,{\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2};\mathcal{P},\mathcal{D}_{t-1})=\sup_{P_{1},P_{2}\in\mathcal{P}}\frac{|P_{1}({\bm{a}}^{1}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}\mid{\bm{x}})-P_{2}({\bm{a}}^{1}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}\mid{\bm{x}})|}{\sqrt{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{1}({\bm{a}}^{1}_{s}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}_{s}\mid{\bm{x}}_{s})-P_{2}({\bm{a}}^{1}_{s}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}_{s}\mid{\bm{x}}_{s}))^{2}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then the eluder dimension of <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d(\mathcal{P},\lambda,T):=\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{a}}^{1}_{1:T},{\bm{a}}^{2}_{1:T}}\sum_{t\in[T]}\min\left\{1,\left[U_{\texttt{GP}}(\lambda,{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}^{1}_{t},{\bm{a}}^{2}_{t};\mathcal{P},\mathcal{D}_{t-1})\right]^{2}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GP</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\mathcal{P},\lambda,T):=\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{a}}^{1}_{1:T},{\bm{a}}^{2}_{1:T}}\sum_{t\in[T]}\min\left\{1,\left[U_{\texttt{GP}}(\lambda,{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}^{1}_{t},{\bm{a}}^{2}_{t};\mathcal{P},\mathcal{D}_{t-1})\right]^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using the standard elliptical potential arguments, we now derive an upper bound for this complexity measure under the GBPM:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS1.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="74.34" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 74.34" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,74.34) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 68.43 C 0 71.69 2.64 74.34 5.91 74.34 L 471.47 74.34 C 474.73 74.34 477.38 71.69 477.38 68.43 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 68.43 C 1.97 70.6 3.73 72.37 5.91 72.37 L 471.47 72.37 C 473.65 72.37 475.41 70.6 475.41 68.43 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 50.95)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:2.69em;font-size:10pt;" height="46.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For GBPM, the eluder dimension <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\mathcal{P},\lambda,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\mathcal{P},\lambda,T)</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded as</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\mathcal{P},\lambda,T)\leq\frac{2d^{2}L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\log\left(1+\frac{4\kappa^{2}S^{2}T}{d^{2}\lambda}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\mathcal{P},\lambda,T)\leq\frac{2d^{2}L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\log\left(1+\frac{4\kappa^{2}S^{2}T}{d^{2}\lambda}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the proof, let us arbitrarily fix a sequence of context-action-action pairs <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{a}}^{1}_{1:T},{\bm{a}}^{2}_{1:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}}_{1:T},{\bm{a}}^{1}_{1:T},{\bm{a}}^{2}_{1:T})</annotation></semantics></math>, and let us denote the induced sequence of features as <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{\phi}_{1:T}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\phi}_{1:T}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{\phi}_{1:T}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\phi}_{1:T}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\phi}_{t}^{i}:=\bm{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}_{t}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\phi}_{t}^{i}:=\bm{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{a}}_{t}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Let us also denote <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Phi}_{t}:=\bm{\phi}_{t}^{1}(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{2})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Phi}_{t}:=\bm{\phi}_{t}^{1}(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{2})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, the induced preference model is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A5.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{\bm{\Theta}}(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{1},\bm{\phi}_{t}^{2}):=\mu\left((\bm{\phi}_{t}^{1})^{\top}\bm{\Theta}\phi_{t}^{2}\right)=\mu\left(\langle\bm{\Theta},\bm{\Phi}_{t}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝚯</mi><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\bm{\Theta}}(\bm{\phi}_{t}^{1},\bm{\phi}_{t}^{2}):=\mu\left((\bm{\phi}_{t}^{1})^{\top}\bm{\Theta}\phi_{t}^{2}\right)=\mu\left(\langle\bm{\Theta},\bm{\Phi}_{t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We bound the uncertainty via the elliptical potential lemma (<a href="#A7.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma G.3 (Elliptical Potential Lemma; Lemma 11 of ( ) ). ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a>).
Let us denote <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}=P_{\bm{\Theta}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}=P_{\bm{\Theta}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some arbitrary <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}_{i}\in\Theta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}_{i}\in\Theta.</annotation></semantics></math>
We first upper bound the numerator as follows:
denoting <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha({\bm{x}},{\bm{\theta}}_{1},{\bm{\theta}}_{2})\coloneqq\int_{0}^{1}\dot{\mu}\bigl({\bm{x}}^{\top}{\bm{\theta}}_{1}+z\,{\bm{x}}^{\top}({\bm{\theta}}_{2}-{\bm{\theta}}_{1})\bigr)\,dz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha({\bm{x}},{\bm{\theta}}_{1},{\bm{\theta}}_{2})\coloneqq\int_{0}^{1}\dot{\mu}\bigl({\bm{x}}^{\top}{\bm{\theta}}_{1}+z\,{\bm{x}}^{\top}({\bm{\theta}}_{2}-{\bm{\theta}}_{1})\bigr)\,dz</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}},{\bm{\theta}}_{1},{\bm{\theta}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}},{\bm{\theta}}_{1},{\bm{\theta}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\mu\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Phi}_{t}\rangle\right)-\mu\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{2},\bm{\Phi}_{t}\rangle\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\mu\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Phi}_{t}\rangle\right)-\mu\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{2},\bm{\Phi}_{t}\rangle\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex118.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=\left|\alpha\!\left(\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{t}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right)\langle\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2},\bm{\Phi}_{t}\rangle\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.473em;" width="0.473em"><mi>α</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=\left|\alpha\!\left(\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{t}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right)\langle\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2},\bm{\Phi}_{t}\rangle\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Mean-value theorem)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=\left|\left\langle\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2},\underbrace{\alpha\!\left(\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{t}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right)\bm{\Phi}_{t}}_{\triangleq\bar{\bm{\Phi}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})}\right\rangle\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.473em;" width="0.473em"><mi>α</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=\left|\left\langle\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2},\underbrace{\alpha\!\left(\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{t}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right)\bm{\Phi}_{t}}_{\triangleq\bar{\bm{\Phi}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})}\right\rangle\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})}\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bar{\bm{\Phi}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2}))\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})^{-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})}\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bar{\bm{\Phi}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2}))\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})^{-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Cauchy-Schwarz inequality)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">for some matrix <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})\succ{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})\succ{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> to be determined later.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the denominator squared:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\left(\mu\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Phi}_{s}\rangle\right)-\mu\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{2},\bm{\Phi}_{s}\rangle\right)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\left(\mu\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Phi}_{s}\rangle\right)-\mu\left(\langle\bm{\Theta}_{2},\bm{\Phi}_{s}\rangle\right)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\left[\alpha\!\left(\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right)^{2}\langle\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2},\bm{\Phi}_{s}\rangle^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.473em;" width="0.473em"><mi>α</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\left[\alpha\!\left(\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right)^{2}\langle\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2},\bm{\Phi}_{s}\rangle^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda+\operatorname{vec}\!\left(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2}\right)^{\top}\left[\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\left(\alpha\!\left(\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right)^{2}\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s})\,\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s})^{\top}\right)\right]\operatorname{vec}\!\left(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.249em;" width="1.249em"><mi>vec</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.473em;" width="0.473em"><mi>α</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.249em;" width="1.249em"><mi>vec</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda+\operatorname{vec}\!\left(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2}\right)^{\top}\left[\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\left(\alpha\!\left(\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right)^{2}\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s})\,\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s})^{\top}\right)\right]\operatorname{vec}\!\left(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})^{\top}\underbrace{\left[\frac{\lambda}{4S^{2}}{\bm{I}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\!\left[\alpha\!\left(\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right)^{2}\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s})\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s})^{\top}\right]\right]}_{\triangleq{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})}\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.473em;" width="0.473em"><mi>α</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})^{\top}\underbrace{\left[\frac{\lambda}{4S^{2}}{\bm{I}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\!\left[\alpha\!\left(\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}),\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right)^{2}\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s})\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\Phi}_{s})^{\top}\right]\right]}_{\triangleq{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})}\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the above two inequalities, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{\texttt{GP}}(\lambda,{\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2};\mathcal{P},\mathcal{D}_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{\texttt{GP}}(\lambda,{\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2};\mathcal{P},\mathcal{D}_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex126.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sup_{\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2}\in\Theta}\frac{\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}}\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bar{\bm{\Phi}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2}))\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})^{-1}}}{\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sup_{\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2}\in\Theta}\frac{\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}}\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bar{\bm{\Phi}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2}))\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})^{-1}}}{\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta}_{1}-\bm{\Theta}_{2})\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2}\in\Theta}\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bar{\bm{\Phi}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2}))\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})^{-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2}\in\Theta}\left\lVert\mathrm{vec}(\bar{\bm{\Phi}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2}))\right\rVert_{{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})^{-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can lower-bound <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> in the Löwner sense using the fact that <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(\cdot,\cdot,\cdot)\geq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(\cdot,\cdot,\cdot)\geq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})\succeq\frac{\lambda}{4S^{2}}{\bm{I}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\kappa^{2}\operatorname{vec}({\bm{\Phi}}_{s})\operatorname{vec}({\bm{\Phi}}_{s})^{\top}=\frac{\lambda}{4S^{2}}{\bm{I}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\operatorname{vec}(\kappa{\bm{\Phi}}_{s})\operatorname{vec}(\kappa{\bm{\Phi}}_{s})^{\top}\triangleq{\bm{V}}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{G}}_{t}(\bm{\Theta}_{1},\bm{\Theta}_{2})\succeq\frac{\lambda}{4S^{2}}{\bm{I}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\kappa^{2}\operatorname{vec}({\bm{\Phi}}_{s})\operatorname{vec}({\bm{\Phi}}_{s})^{\top}=\frac{\lambda}{4S^{2}}{\bm{I}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\operatorname{vec}(\kappa{\bm{\Phi}}_{s})\operatorname{vec}(\kappa{\bm{\Phi}}_{s})^{\top}\triangleq{\bm{V}}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, as <math id="A5.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(\cdot,\cdot,\cdot)\leq L_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(\cdot,\cdot,\cdot)\leq L_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A5.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\texttt{GP}}(\lambda,{\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2};\mathcal{P},\mathcal{D}_{t-1})\leq\frac{L_{\mu}}{\kappa}\left\lVert\operatorname{vec}(\kappa\bm{\Phi}_{t})\right\rVert_{{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\texttt{GP}}(\lambda,{\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2};\mathcal{P},\mathcal{D}_{t-1})\leq\frac{L_{\mu}}{\kappa}\left\lVert\operatorname{vec}(\kappa\bm{\Phi}_{t})\right\rVert_{{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">We then conclude the proof via the elliptical potential lemma (<a href="#A7.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma G.3 (Elliptical Potential Lemma; Lemma 11 of ( ) ). ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d({\mathcal{P}},\lambda,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d({\mathcal{P}},\lambda,T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex129.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\min\left\{1,\frac{L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\left\lVert\operatorname{vec}(\kappa\bm{\Phi}_{t})\right\rVert_{{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}}^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\min\left\{1,\frac{L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\left\lVert\operatorname{vec}(\kappa\bm{\Phi}_{t})\right\rVert_{{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}}^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex130.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\min\left\{1,\left\lVert\operatorname{vec}(\kappa\bm{\Phi}_{t})\right\rVert_{{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}}^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\min\left\{1,\left\lVert\operatorname{vec}(\kappa\bm{\Phi}_{t})\right\rVert_{{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}}^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A5.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\leq L_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\leq L_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2d^{2}L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\log\left(1+\frac{4\kappa^{2}S^{2}T}{d^{2}\lambda}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2d^{2}L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\log\left(1+\frac{4\kappa^{2}S^{2}T}{d^{2}\lambda}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Connection to the Standard Eluder Dimensions</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix, we will elucidate the connection between <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition E.1 (Eluder dimension, General Preference Model ( , )). ‣ E.1 Upper Bounding the Eluder Dimension of ( ) ‣ Appendix E Eluder Dimension of GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> and two other “standard” definitions of eluder-type complexities: <em id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sequential extrapolation coefficient (SEC)</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib92" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and the original eluder dimension <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">Russo and Van Roy, 2013</a>)</cite>
For simplicity, we denote <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Z}}:={\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}\times{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Z}}:={\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}\times{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P({\bm{z}}):=P({\bm{a}}^{1}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}\mid{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P({\bm{z}}):=P({\bm{a}}^{1}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}\mid{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}=({\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}=({\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we recall the definition of SEC adopted for our setting:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition E.3</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>-regularized SEC, Definition 7 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib92" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al. (2023)</a></cite>)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi\subseteq\Delta({\mathcal{Z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi\subseteq\Delta({\mathcal{Z}})</annotation></semantics></math> be a distribution class. Then, the SEC is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},\Pi,T):=\sup_{P_{1:T}^{1},P_{1:T}^{2}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}}\ \sup_{\nu_{1:T}\subseteq\Pi}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\left(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{t}\sim\nu_{t}}[P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{t})]\right)^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{s}\sim\nu_{s}}\big[(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}\big]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>SEC</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></munder><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},\Pi,T):=\sup_{P_{1:T}^{1},P_{1:T}^{2}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}}\ \sup_{\nu_{1:T}\subseteq\Pi}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\left(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{t}\sim\nu_{t}}[P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{t})]\right)^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{s}\sim\nu_{s}}\big[(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}\big]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note that when the distribution class is restricted to the set of Dirac measures <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{D}}:=\{\delta_{{\bm{z}}}:{\bm{z}}\in Z\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝒛</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{D}}:=\{\delta_{{\bm{z}}}:{\bm{z}}\in Z\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following relationship between SEC and <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition E.1 (Eluder dimension, General Preference Model ( , )). ‣ E.1 Upper Bounding the Eluder Dimension of ( ) ‣ Appendix E Eluder Dimension of GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d({\mathcal{P}},\lambda,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d({\mathcal{P}},\lambda,T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex133.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{{\bm{z}}_{1:T}}\sum_{t\in[T]}\min\left\{1,\sup_{P_{1},P_{2}\in\mathcal{P}}\frac{(P_{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{2}({\bm{z}}_{t}))^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{2}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{{\bm{z}}_{1:T}}\sum_{t\in[T]}\min\left\{1,\sup_{P_{1},P_{2}\in\mathcal{P}}\frac{(P_{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{2}({\bm{z}}_{t}))^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{2}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sup_{{\bm{z}}_{1:T}}\sum_{t\in[T]}\sup_{P_{1},P_{2}\in\mathcal{P}}\frac{(P_{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{2}({\bm{z}}_{t}))^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{2}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sup_{{\bm{z}}_{1:T}}\sum_{t\in[T]}\sup_{P_{1},P_{2}\in\mathcal{P}}\frac{(P_{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{2}({\bm{z}}_{t}))^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{2}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{P_{1:T}^{1},P_{1:T}^{2}}\sup_{{\bm{z}}_{1:T}}\sum_{t\in[T]}\frac{(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{t}))^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{s}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{s}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{P_{1:T}^{1},P_{1:T}^{2}}\sup_{{\bm{z}}_{1:T}}\sum_{t\in[T]}\frac{(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{t}))^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{s}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{s}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{P_{1:T}^{1},P_{1:T}^{2}}\sup_{\nu_{1:T}\subseteq{\bm{D}}}\sum_{t\in[T]}\frac{(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{t}\sim\nu_{t}}[P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{t})])^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{s}\sim\nu_{s}}[P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{s})])^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{P_{1:T}^{1},P_{1:T}^{2}}\sup_{\nu_{1:T}\subseteq{\bm{D}}}\sum_{t\in[T]}\frac{(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{t}\sim\nu_{t}}[P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{t})])^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{s}\sim\nu_{s}}[P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{s})])^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>SEC</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Second, we recall the standard eluder dimension of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib93" title="" class="ltx_ref">Foster et al. (2021)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib94" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2022a)</a></cite>:<span id="footnote10" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">10</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            The original definition is due to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">Russo and Van Roy (2013)</a></cite> and slightly different, but as mentioned in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib94" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2022a)</a></cite>, the “new” definition is “never larger and is sufficient to analyze all the applications of eluder dimension in literature.”</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition E.4</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Definition 1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib94" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2022a)</a></cite>)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any fixed preference <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{*}\in{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{*}\in{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and scale <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the <span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">exact eluder dimension</span> <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}_{P^{*}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Edim</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}_{P^{*}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> is the largest <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that there exists a sequence <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{({\bm{z}}_{t},P_{t})\}_{t\in[m]}\subset{\mathcal{Z}}\times{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{({\bm{z}}_{t},P_{t})\}_{t\in[m]}\subset{\mathcal{Z}}\times{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following holds:
for all <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|P_{t}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{t})\right|&gt;\varepsilon,\quad\text{and}\quad\sum_{s&lt;t}\left(P_{t}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{s})\right)^{2}&lt;\varepsilon^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|P_{t}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{t})\right|&gt;\varepsilon,\quad\text{and}\quad\sum_{s&lt;t}\left(P_{t}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{s})\right)^{2}&lt;\varepsilon^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for all <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define:</span></p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The </span><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">eluder dimension</span><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Edim}_{P^{*}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon):=\sup_{\varepsilon^{\prime}\geq\varepsilon}\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}_{P^{*}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Edim</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Edim</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Edim}_{P^{*}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon):=\sup_{\varepsilon^{\prime}\geq\varepsilon}\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}_{P^{*}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon):=\sup_{P^{*}\in{\mathcal{P}}}\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}_{P^{*}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Edim</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Edim</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon):=\sup_{P^{*}\in{\mathcal{P}}}\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}_{P^{*}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon):=\sup_{P^{*}\in{\mathcal{P}}}\mathrm{Edim}_{P^{*}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Edim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Edim</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon):=\sup_{P^{*}\in{\mathcal{P}}}\mathrm{Edim}_{P^{*}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We first prove that <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Edim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>SEC</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)</annotation></semantics></math> are equivalent up to some constants and logarithmic factors:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="90.44" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 90.44" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,90.44) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 84.53 C 0 87.8 2.64 90.44 5.91 90.44 L 471.47 90.44 C 474.73 90.44 477.38 87.8 477.38 84.53 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 84.53 C 1.97 86.71 3.73 88.47 5.91 88.47 L 471.47 88.47 C 473.65 88.47 475.41 86.71 475.41 84.53 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 67.05)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:3.85em;font-size:10pt;" height="62.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition E.5</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Suppose that <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Z}}\subseteq{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒵</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Z}}\subseteq{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta\subseteq\mathrm{Skew}(d;2r,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta\subseteq\mathrm{Skew}(d;2r,S)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\geq\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Edim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then,</span></span>
<span id="A5.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\varepsilon^{2}\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)}{\lambda+\varepsilon^{2}}\leq\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)\lesssim\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},T^{-1/2})\log T." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Edim</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">SEC</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≲</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Edim</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\varepsilon^{2}\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)}{\lambda+\varepsilon^{2}}\leq\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)\lesssim\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},T^{-1/2})\log T.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove each direction separately.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Upper Bound.<span id="A5.SS2.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Noting that for <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)\leq\mathrm{SEC}_{1}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>SEC</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>SEC</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)\leq\mathrm{SEC}_{1}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)</annotation></semantics></math>, this immediately follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib92" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al. (2023, Proposition 7)</a></cite> with <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}={\bm{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}={\bm{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lower Bound.<span id="A5.SS2.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Consider the eluder witness, i.e., a sequence of <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{({\bm{z}}_{t},P_{t})\}_{t\in{d_{e}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{({\bm{z}}_{t},P_{t})\}_{t\in{d_{e}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and some fixed preference <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that attains the eluder dimension <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{e}:=\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Edim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{e}:=\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, by definition,</span></span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>SEC</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{SEC}_{\lambda}({\mathcal{P}},{\bm{D}},T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex138.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{P_{1:T}^{1},P_{1:T}^{2}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}}\ \sup_{{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\subseteq{\mathcal{Z}}}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\left(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{t})\right)^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{P_{1:T}^{1},P_{1:T}^{2}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}}\ \sup_{{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\subseteq{\mathcal{Z}}}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\left(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{t})\right)^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P_{t}^{2}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex139.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sup_{P_{1:T}^{1}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}}\ \sup_{{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\subseteq{\mathcal{Z}}}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\left(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{t})\right)^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sup_{P_{1:T}^{1}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}}\ \sup_{{\bm{z}}_{1:T}\subseteq{\mathcal{Z}}}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\left(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{t})\right)^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{t}^{1}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Set <math id="A5.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}^{2}=P^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}^{2}=P^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.Ex139.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex140.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{t=1}^{d_{e}}\frac{\left(P_{t}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{t})\right)^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{t}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{t=1}^{d_{e}}\frac{\left(P_{t}({\bm{z}}_{t})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{t})\right)^{2}}{\lambda+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}(P_{t}({\bm{z}}_{s})-P^{*}({\bm{z}}_{s}))^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Set <math id="A5.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Ex140.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P^{1}_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{1}_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the eluder witness sequence)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\sum_{t=1}^{d_{e}}\frac{\varepsilon^{2}}{\lambda+\varepsilon^{2}}=\frac{d_{e}\varepsilon^{2}}{\lambda+\varepsilon^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\sum_{t=1}^{d_{e}}\frac{\varepsilon^{2}}{\lambda+\varepsilon^{2}}=\frac{d_{e}\varepsilon^{2}}{\lambda+\varepsilon^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We conclude with a nearly-tight characterization of the eluder dimension of GBPM, whose proof is deferred to the next subsection:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.p11.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="243.72" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 243.72" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,243.72) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 237.82 C 0 241.08 2.64 243.72 5.91 243.72 L 471.47 243.72 C 474.73 243.72 477.38 241.08 477.38 237.82 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 237.82 C 1.97 239.99 3.73 241.76 5.91 241.76 L 471.47 241.76 C 473.65 241.76 475.41 239.99 475.41 237.82 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 220.34)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:14.93em;font-size:10pt;" height="216.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.SS2.p11.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition E.6</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}\subseteq{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒳</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}\subseteq{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta\subseteq\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta\subseteq\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the function class as the <span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GBPM</span>:</span></span>
<span id="A5.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}:=\left\{({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}})\mapsto\mu\left({\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}\right):\bm{\Theta}\in\Theta\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒚</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚯</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}:=\left\{({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}})\mapsto\mu\left({\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}\right):\bm{\Theta}\in\Theta\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where we have the following properties: <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\leq\dot{\mu}({\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}})\leq L_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐲</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\leq\dot{\mu}({\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}})\leq L_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|{\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}\right|\leq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐲</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|{\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}\right|\leq S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote11" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">11</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">11</sup>
                                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">11</span></span>
                                
                                
                                
                                
                                
                                
                                
                              <span id="footnote11.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This follows from matrix Hölder inequality: </span><math id="footnote11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|{\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}\right|=\left|\langle\bm{\Theta},{\bm{x}}{\bm{y}}^{\top}\rangle\right|\leq\left\lVert\bm{\Theta}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}}\left\lVert{\bm{x}}{\bm{y}}^{\top}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐲</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚯</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐲</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">‖</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚯</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">‖</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">nuc</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">‖</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐲</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">‖</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">op</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|{\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}\right|=\left|\langle\bm{\Theta},{\bm{x}}{\bm{y}}^{\top}\rangle\right|\leq\left\lVert\bm{\Theta}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}}\left\lVert{\bm{x}}{\bm{y}}^{\top}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leq S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote11.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span></span></span> for all <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}},\bm{\Theta})\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\times\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐲</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚯</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒳</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒳</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}},\bm{\Theta})\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\times\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, its eluder dimension is bounded as follows: for any <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&lt;SL_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&lt;SL_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></span>
<span id="A5.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)\leq\frac{3e}{e-1}\cdot d^{2}\cdot\frac{L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\cdot\log\frac{24S^{2}L_{\mu}^{2}}{\varepsilon^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Edim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)\leq\frac{3e}{e-1}\cdot d^{2}\cdot\frac{L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\cdot\log\frac{24S^{2}L_{\mu}^{2}}{\varepsilon^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Furthermore, if <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(z)=\frac{1}{2}+z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(z)=\frac{1}{2}+z</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have the following lower bound:</span></span>
<span id="A5.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)\geq\binom{d}{2}\log_{4}\frac{S}{\sqrt{3}\varepsilon}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Edim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" linethickness="0pt" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Edim}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)\geq\binom{d}{2}\log_{4}\frac{S}{\sqrt{3}\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the same <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Omega}(d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Omega}(d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> lower bound applies to the SEC due to <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition E.5. ‣ E.2 Connection to the Standard Eluder Dimensions ‣ Appendix E Eluder Dimension of GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a>.
This <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Omega}(d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Omega}(d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> scaling implies that eluder-dimension-based frameworks cannot efficiently exploit the low-rank structure of <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The high eluder dimension arises because <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Skew}(d;2r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Skew}(d;2r)</annotation></semantics></math> contains rank-<math id="A5.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> “coordinate spikes” of the form <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{e}}_{i}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}-{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{i}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{e}}_{i}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}-{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{i}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math>.
An adversary can query specific pairs to isolate these directions one-by-one.
Since the eluder dimension measures worst-case separability rather than metric entropy (which scales as <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(dr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(dr)</annotation></semantics></math>), it reflects the ambient basis size even when the parameter manifold is low-dimensional.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">This limitation is best understood through the “global embedding” characterization.
Specifically, a standard sufficient condition for bounding the eluder dimension by the <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-rank relies on constructing <em id="A5.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">global</em> maps <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\to{\mathcal{B}}^{d_{e}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\to{\mathcal{B}}^{d_{e}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w:\Theta\to{\mathcal{B}}^{d_{e}}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w:\Theta\to{\mathcal{B}}^{d_{e}}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}=\langle\phi({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}),w(\bm{\Theta})\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}=\langle\phi({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}),w(\bm{\Theta})\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib94" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2022a</a>, Proposition 4)</cite>.
While skew-symmetry admits a Schur decomposition <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}={\bm{Q}}\bm{\Lambda}{\bm{Q}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}={\bm{Q}}\bm{\Lambda}{\bm{Q}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> that allows the representation</p>
<table id="A5.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}=\Big\langle\mathrm{vec}\big(({\bm{Q}}^{\top}{\bm{x}})({\bm{Q}}^{\top}{\bm{y}})^{\top}\big),\,\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Lambda})\Big\rangle," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}{\bm{y}}=\Big\langle\mathrm{vec}\big(({\bm{Q}}^{\top}{\bm{x}})({\bm{Q}}^{\top}{\bm{y}})^{\top}\big),\,\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Lambda})\Big\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p">this does not yield a valid low-dimensional witness.
Crucially, the feature map depends on the basis <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> (and thus on the specific parameter <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math>), which violates the condition of having a single global feature map across the entire hypothesis class.
Consequently, guarantees relying on such complexity measures (e.g., <span id="A5.SS2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GS</span> by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a)</a></cite>) incur the full <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> complexity, mirroring the statistical hardness of quadratic functions with full-rank Hessians <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">Osband and Van Roy, 2014</a>, Proposition 3)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition E.6. ‣ E.2 Connection to the Standard Eluder Dimensions ‣ Appendix E Eluder Dimension of GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the proof, we recall the notion of <em id="A5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">generalized rank</em> and a useful proposition linking the above two concepts:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition E.7</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Definition 3 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib94" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2022a)</a></cite>)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a given <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:{\mathbb{R}}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:{\mathbb{R}}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-rank</span> of <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> at scale <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted as <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\text{-}\mathrm{rk}({\mathcal{P}},R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\text{-}\mathrm{rk}({\mathcal{P}},R)</annotation></semantics></math>, is the smallest dimension <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> for which there exist <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\phi},R_{w}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\phi},R_{w}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\phi}R_{w}=R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\phi}R_{w}=R</annotation></semantics></math>, and (global) mappings <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\rightarrow{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(R_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\rightarrow{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(R_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w:{\mathcal{P}}\rightarrow{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(R_{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w:{\mathcal{P}}\rightarrow{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(R_{w})</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A5.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P({\bm{x}}\succ{\bm{y}})=\mu\left(\langle\phi({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}),w(P)\rangle\right),\quad\forall({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}},P)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{P}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>≻</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P({\bm{x}}\succ{\bm{y}})=\mu\left(\langle\phi({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}),w(P)\rangle\right),\quad\forall({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}},P)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{P}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">or <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math> if no such <math id="A5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> exists.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition E.8</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Proposition 4(ii) of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib94" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2022a)</a></cite>)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="A5.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&lt;RL_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&lt;RL_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)\leq\frac{3e}{e-1}\cdot\mu\text{-}\mathrm{rk}({\mathcal{P}})\cdot\frac{L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\cdot\log\frac{24R^{2}L_{\mu}^{2}}{\varepsilon^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Edim</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)\leq\frac{3e}{e-1}\cdot\mu\text{-}\mathrm{rk}({\mathcal{P}})\cdot\frac{L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\cdot\log\frac{24R^{2}L_{\mu}^{2}}{\varepsilon^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We prove the upper and lower bounds separately.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Upper Bound.</span>
This follows trivially from adapting <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem8" title="Proposition E.8 (Proposition 4(ii) of ( ) ). ‣ E.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix E Eluder Dimension of GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.8</span></a> to our setting by considering <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}})\mapsto\mathrm{vec}({\bm{x}}{\bm{y}}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}})\mapsto\mathrm{vec}({\bm{x}}{\bm{y}}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w:\bm{\Theta}\mapsto\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w:\bm{\Theta}\mapsto\mathrm{vec}(\bm{\Theta})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lower Bound.</span>
The construction is largely inspired by that of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib94" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2022a, Proposition 5)</a></cite>, which we adapt to our setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We will construct a sequence <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}_{t},\bm{\Theta}_{t})\}_{t\in[m]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{({\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}_{t},\bm{\Theta}_{t})\}_{t\in[m]}</annotation></semantics></math> that witnesses the claimed lower bound with <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}_{\star}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}_{\star}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The key observation is that <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Skew}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Skew}(d)</annotation></semantics></math> admits the following orthonormal basis: <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}\triangleq\left\{\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}({\bm{e}}_{i}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}-{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{i}^{\top})\right\}_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>≜</mo><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}\triangleq\left\{\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}({\bm{e}}_{i}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}-{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{i}^{\top})\right\}_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For given <math id="A5.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A5.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(\varepsilon,\sqrt{3}\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(\varepsilon,\sqrt{3}\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k:=\lfloor\log_{4}\frac{S}{\alpha}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k:=\lfloor\log_{4}\frac{S}{\alpha}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we can first consider the following sequence of length <math id="A5.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1</annotation></semantics></math>: for <math id="A5.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0\}\cup[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0\}\cup[k]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}=2^{t-k}{\bm{e}}_{1},\ {\bm{y}}_{t}=2^{t-k}{\bm{e}}_{2},\quad\bm{\Theta}_{t}=\alpha\cdot 2^{2(k-t)}({\bm{e}}_{1}{\bm{e}}_{2}^{\top}-{\bm{e}}_{2}{\bm{e}}_{1}^{\top})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}=2^{t-k}{\bm{e}}_{1},\ {\bm{y}}_{t}=2^{t-k}{\bm{e}}_{2},\quad\bm{\Theta}_{t}=\alpha\cdot 2^{2(k-t)}({\bm{e}}_{1}{\bm{e}}_{2}^{\top}-{\bm{e}}_{2}{\bm{e}}_{1}^{\top}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A5.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu({\bm{x}}_{t}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{t}{\bm{y}}_{t})-\mu(0)={\bm{x}}_{t}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{t}{\bm{y}}_{t}=\alpha&gt;\varepsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu({\bm{x}}_{t}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{t}{\bm{y}}_{t})-\mu(0)={\bm{x}}_{t}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{t}{\bm{y}}_{t}=\alpha&gt;\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A5.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{s&lt;t}\left(\mu({\bm{x}}_{s}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{t}{\bm{y}}_{s})-\mu(0)\right)=\sum_{s&lt;t}{\bm{x}}_{s}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{t}{\bm{y}}_{s}=\alpha\sum_{s&lt;t}2^{2s-2t}&lt;\frac{1}{3}\alpha&lt;\varepsilon^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{s&lt;t}\left(\mu({\bm{x}}_{s}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{t}{\bm{y}}_{s})-\mu(0)\right)=\sum_{s&lt;t}{\bm{x}}_{s}^{\top}\bm{\Theta}_{t}{\bm{y}}_{s}=\alpha\sum_{s&lt;t}2^{2s-2t}&lt;\frac{1}{3}\alpha&lt;\varepsilon^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p6.4" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A5.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t}\in{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{t}\in{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\bm{\Theta}_{t}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}}\leq\alpha 2^{2k}\leq\alpha 4^{\log_{4}\frac{S}{\alpha}}=S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>nuc</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\bm{\Theta}_{t}\right\rVert_{\mathrm{nuc}}\leq\alpha 2^{2k}\leq\alpha 4^{\log_{4}\frac{S}{\alpha}}=S</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A5.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)\geq k+1\geq\log_{4}\frac{S}{\alpha}\geq\log_{4}\frac{S}{\sqrt{3}\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Edim</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\mathrm{Edim}}({\mathcal{P}},\varepsilon)\geq k+1\geq\log_{4}\frac{S}{\alpha}\geq\log_{4}\frac{S}{\sqrt{3}\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Now we concatenate <math id="A5.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{d}{2}=\frac{d(d+1)}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{d}{2}=\frac{d(d+1)}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> times across the basis <math id="A5.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A5.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t,i,j}=2^{t-k}{\bm{e}}_{i},\ {\bm{y}}_{t,i,j}=2^{t-k}{\bm{e}}_{j},\quad\bm{\Theta}_{t,i,j}=\alpha\cdot 2^{2(k-t)}({\bm{e}}_{i}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}-{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{i}^{\top})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t,i,j}=2^{t-k}{\bm{e}}_{i},\ {\bm{y}}_{t,i,j}=2^{t-k}{\bm{e}}_{j},\quad\bm{\Theta}_{t,i,j}=\alpha\cdot 2^{2(k-t)}({\bm{e}}_{i}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}-{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{i}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A5.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i&lt;j\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i&lt;j\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>, and we are done.
∎</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Instantiating Regret Bound of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a)</a></cite> to GBPM</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Regret Bound of <span id="A6.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Greedy Sampling</span></h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For this section, we will consider the reverse KL-regularization as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a)</a></cite>, i.e., <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\pi)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\pi)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math> for some fixed <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that we defined the regularized and unregularized Max-Best-Response Regrets as</p>
<table id="A6.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T):=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left\{\frac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\right\},\quad\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T):=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left\{\frac{1}{2}-J(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T):=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left\{\frac{1}{2}-J_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\right\},\quad\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T):=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left\{\frac{1}{2}-J(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we derive the regularized and unregularized regret bound of <span id="A6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Greedy Sampling (GS)</span> of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a)</a></cite> for GBPM, based on general function approximation. We first recall the regret bound from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a)</a></cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem F.1</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem 1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a)</a></cite>)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the preference class <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite with cardinality <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathcal{P}}=|{\mathcal{P}}|&lt;\infty." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathcal{P}}=|{\mathcal{P}}|&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math>
For any <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GS</span> attains the following regret bound:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}}(T)=O\left({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{\eta}}\,d(\mathcal{P},\lambda,T)\log(N_{\mathcal{P}}T/\delta)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">e</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}}(T)=O\left({\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{\eta}}\,d(\mathcal{P},\lambda,T)\log(N_{\mathcal{P}}T/\delta)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Instantiation for GBPM.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first instantiate the KL-regularized regret bound for GBPM:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="140.75" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 140.75" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,140.75) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 134.85 C 0 138.11 2.64 140.75 5.91 140.75 L 471.47 140.75 C 474.73 140.75 477.38 138.11 477.38 134.85 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 134.85 C 1.97 137.02 3.73 138.78 5.91 138.78 L 471.47 138.78 C 473.65 138.78 475.41 137.02 475.41 134.85 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 117.36)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:7.49em;font-size:10pt;" height="113.2" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem F.2</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(KL-regularized Regret Bound of <span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Greedy Sampling</span>)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For any <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability with at least <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GS</span> (when applied to <span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GBPM</span>) attains the following regret bound:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex147" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)\lesssim{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{\eta}}\cdot\frac{d^{2}L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\cdot\log T\cdot\left(\log\frac{T}{\delta}+dr\log(LST)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≲</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">e</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)\lesssim{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{\eta}}\cdot\frac{d^{2}L_{\mu}^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\cdot\log T\cdot\left(\log\frac{T}{\delta}+dr\log(LST)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof consists of two parts: 1) Extending the preference model class size term for the infinite preference space, and 2) Bounding the eluder dimension of </span><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">GBPM</span><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text">.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first extend the term <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathcal{P}}=|{\mathcal{P}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathcal{P}}=|{\mathcal{P}}|</annotation></semantics></math> for the infinite space case <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta\triangleq\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta\triangleq\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)</annotation></semantics></math> by using covering number arguments.
We denote <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\bm{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\bm{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the preference probability given by </span><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">GBPM</span><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text"> for parameter <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For simplicity, we use the following notations introduced in the previous section. We denote <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Z}}:={\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}\times{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Z}}:={\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}\times{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P({\bm{z}}):=P({\bm{a}}^{1}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}\mid{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P({\bm{z}}):=P({\bm{a}}^{1}\succ{\bm{a}}^{2}\mid{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}=({\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}=({\bm{x}},{\bm{a}}^{1},{\bm{a}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using these, we have the following lemma, whose proof is provided in <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Proof of : MLE Estimator Bound ‣ Appendix F Instantiating Regret Bound of ( ) to GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.3</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{({\bm{z}}_{i},r_{i})\}_{i\in[t]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{({\bm{z}}_{i},r_{i})\}_{i\in[t]}</annotation></semantics></math> be a potentially adaptively collected data with <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\sim\mathrm{Ber}(P({\bm{z}}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Ber</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\sim\mathrm{Ber}(P({\bm{z}}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote the (constrained) MLE as <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}:=\argmax_{\bm{\Theta}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)}\sum_{i\in[t]}\ell_{i}(\bm{\Theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Skew</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}:=\argmax_{\bm{\Theta}\in\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)}\sum_{i\in[t]}\ell_{i}(\bm{\Theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}(\bm{\Theta}):=\left(r_{i}\log P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})+(1-r_{i})\log(1-P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}(\bm{\Theta}):=\left(r_{i}\log P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})+(1-r_{i})\log(1-P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose that <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz w.r.t. the Frobenius norm.
Then, for any <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> the following holds:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\lesssim\log\frac{T}{\delta}+dr\log LST\right)\geq 1-\delta,\quad\forall t\in[T]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\lesssim\log\frac{T}{\delta}+dr\log LST\right)\geq 1-\delta,\quad\forall t\in[T].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">With this lemma and our eluder dimension bound (<a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition E.2. ‣ E.1 Upper Bounding the Eluder Dimension of ( ) ‣ Appendix E Eluder Dimension of GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a>), the derivation of the regret bound in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a)</a></cite> follows through, with <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\left(\frac{N_{\mathcal{P}}T}{\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\left(\frac{N_{\mathcal{P}}T}{\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> both replaced with <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{T}{\delta}+dr\log LST" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{T}{\delta}+dr\log LST</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Converting to Unregularized Regret Bound.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now convert the KL-regularized regret bound to its unregularized counterpart via the following lemma:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.4</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{ref}}:=\max_{\pi\in\Pi}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{ref}}:=\max_{\pi\in\Pi}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)\leq\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{ref}}T." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)\leq\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{ref}}T.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the KL-regularized objective is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}}(\pi,\pi^{\prime})=J(\pi,\pi^{\prime})-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi^{\prime},\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}}(\pi,\pi^{\prime})=J(\pi,\pi^{\prime})-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi^{\prime},\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex151"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left(\frac{1}{2}-J(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left(\frac{1}{2}-J(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left(\frac{1}{2}-\left(J(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left(\frac{1}{2}-\left(J(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left(\frac{1}{2}-J_{{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\right)+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left(-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left(\frac{1}{2}-J_{{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi)\right)+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\left(-{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\hat{\pi}_{t}^{1},\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex155"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{ref}}T." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}_{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}(T)+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{ref}}T.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Putting everything together, we have the following corollary of <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem F.2 (KL-regularized Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling). ‣ Instantiation for GBPM. ‣ F.1 Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Appendix F Instantiating Regret Bound of ( ) to GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a> for the unregularized regret bound:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="188.97" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 188.97" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,188.97) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 183.06 C 0 186.32 2.64 188.97 5.91 188.97 L 471.47 188.97 C 474.73 188.97 477.38 186.32 477.38 183.06 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 183.06 C 1.97 185.24 3.73 187 5.91 187 L 471.47 187 C 473.65 187 475.41 185.24 475.41 183.06 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 166.68)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:11.05em;font-size:10pt;" height="161.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary F.5</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unregularized Regret Bound of <span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GS</span>)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Suppose <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{ref}}:=\max_{\pi\in\Pi}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ref</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ref</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{ref}}:=\max_{\pi\in\Pi}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Then with probability at least <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the unregularized regret of <span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GS</span> under <span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GBPM</span> satisfies</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)\lesssim{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{\eta}}d^{2}\kappa^{-2}L_{\mu}^{2}\cdot\log T\cdot\left(\log\frac{T}{\delta}+dr\log(LST)\right)+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{ref}}T." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">MBR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Reg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">e</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MBR\text{-}Reg}(T)\lesssim{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{\eta}}d^{2}\kappa^{-2}L_{\mu}^{2}\cdot\log T\cdot\left(\log\frac{T}{\delta}+dr\log(LST)\right)+{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{ref}}T.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Furthermore, there exists no <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> (even dependent on <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>) such that the RHS is <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(T^{1-\gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(T^{1-\gamma})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The regret bound is a direct result from the KL-regularized regret bound in <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem F.2 (KL-regularized Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling). ‣ Instantiation for GBPM. ‣ F.1 Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Appendix F Instantiating Regret Bound of ( ) to GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>, converted to unregularized regret via <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma F.4. ‣ Converting to Unregularized Regret Bound. ‣ F.1 Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Appendix F Instantiating Regret Bound of ( ) to GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.4</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the second claim,
suppose that this is true. Then, for the second term, we require <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{ref}}T={\mathcal{O}}(T^{1-\gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta^{-1}}D_{\mathrm{ref}}T={\mathcal{O}}(T^{1-\gamma})</annotation></semantics></math> to hold, which implies <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}=\Omega(T^{\gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}\eta}=\Omega(T^{\gamma})</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging this into the first term leads to an additive term of <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(e^{T^{\gamma}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(e^{T^{\gamma}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is superpolynomial: a contradiction. This concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma F.3. ‣ Proof. ‣ Instantiation for GBPM. ‣ F.1 Regret Bound of Greedy Sampling ‣ Appendix F Instantiating Regret Bound of ( ) to GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>: MLE Estimator Bound</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define the probability mass function (pmf) of <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\mid{\bm{z}}\sim\mathrm{Ber}(P({\bm{z}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Ber</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\mid{\bm{z}}\sim\mathrm{Ber}(P({\bm{z}}))</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A6.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(r\mid{\bm{z}})=P({\bm{z}})^{r}(1-P({\bm{z}}))^{1-r},\quad r\in\{0,1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(r\mid{\bm{z}})=P({\bm{z}})^{r}(1-P({\bm{z}}))^{1-r},\quad r\in\{0,1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then we have the following lemma, whose proof is deferred to <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Instantiating Regret Bound of ( ) to GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.6</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each <math id="A6.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>, the following holds:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\leq\log\frac{1}{\delta}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}\right)\geq 1-\delta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\leq\log\frac{1}{\delta}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}\right)\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net of <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the Frobenius norm.
Then by the union bound, we have:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\leq\log\frac{|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|}{\delta}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})},\quad\forall\bm{\Theta}\in\Theta_{\varepsilon}\right)\geq 1-\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\leq\log\frac{|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|}{\delta}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})},\quad\forall\bm{\Theta}\in\Theta_{\varepsilon}\right)\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the epsilon net element corresponding to <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
i.e., <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}-\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}\rVert_{F}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}-\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}\rVert_{F}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\leq\log\frac{|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|}{\delta}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}\right)\geq 1-\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\leq\log\frac{|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|}{\delta}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}\right)\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Using the inequality <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a-b)^{2}\geq\frac{1}{2}(a-c)^{2}-(b-c)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a-b)^{2}\geq\frac{1}{2}(a-c)^{2}-(b-c)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the optimality of the MLE, with probability at least <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> the following holds:</p>
<table id="A6.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex161"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}-\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}-\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex162"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|}{\delta}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|}{\delta}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex163"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\frac{|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|}{\delta}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\frac{|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|}{\delta}+\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now, note that for any <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex164" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})=r_{i}\log P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})+(1-r_{i})\log(1-P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})=r_{i}\log P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})+(1-r_{i})\log(1-P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">which is <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz in <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> by given.
With this, we can bound the log sum on the right as</p>
<table id="A6.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}\leq Lt\left\lVert\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}-\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}\right\rVert_{F}\leq Lt\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}\leq Lt\left\lVert\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}-\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}\right\rVert_{F}\leq Lt\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since we assumed that <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P_{\bm{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P_{\bm{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, it follows that <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\bm{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\bm{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> is also <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz.<span id="footnote12" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">12</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">12</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">12</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            As the Lipschitz constant is the maximum gradient norm by the Rademacher’s theorem, <math id="footnote12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\nabla_{\bm{\Theta}}P_{\bm{\Theta}}\right\rVert=P_{\bm{\Theta}}\cdot\left\lVert\nabla_{\bm{\Theta}}\log P_{\bm{\Theta}}\right\rVert\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\nabla_{\bm{\Theta}}P_{\bm{\Theta}}\right\rVert=P_{\bm{\Theta}}\cdot\left\lVert\nabla_{\bm{\Theta}}\log P_{\bm{\Theta}}\right\rVert\leq L</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span> Therefore,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\leq Lt\varepsilon^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{\varepsilon,t}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\leq Lt\varepsilon^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We now bound the cardinality of the <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|</annotation></semantics></math> by bounding the covering number of a slightly larger set:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.7</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma 3.1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Candès and Plan (2011)</a></cite>)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Theta(d,2r;S)\coloneqq\{{\bm{X}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d\times d}\mid\|\mathbf{X}\|_{F}\leq S,\operatorname{rank}({\bm{X}})\leq 2r\}\supseteq\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>rank</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊇</mo><mi>Skew</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(d,2r;S)\coloneqq\{{\bm{X}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d\times d}\mid\|\mathbf{X}\|_{F}\leq S,\operatorname{rank}({\bm{X}})\leq 2r\}\supseteq\mathrm{Skew}(d,2r;S)</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A6.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an <math id="A6.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-net <math id="A6.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A6.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(d,2r;S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(d,2r;S)</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="A6.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|\leq\left(\frac{9S}{\varepsilon}\right)^{2(2d+1)r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Theta_{\varepsilon}|\leq\left(\frac{9S}{\varepsilon}\right)^{2(2d+1)r}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Putting the bounds together, we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A6.Ex167" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\lesssim\log\frac{1}{\delta}+Lt\varepsilon+Lt\varepsilon^{2}+dr\log\frac{S}{\varepsilon}\right)\geq 1-\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\lesssim\log\frac{1}{\delta}+Lt\varepsilon+Lt\varepsilon^{2}+dr\log\frac{S}{\varepsilon}\right)\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Choosing <math id="A6.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\approx\frac{1}{(Lt)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\approx\frac{1}{(Lt)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex168" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\lesssim\log\frac{1}{\delta}+dr\log(LSt)\right)\geq 1-\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\lesssim\log\frac{1}{\delta}+dr\log(LSt)\right)\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Setting <math id="A6.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\delta/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\delta/T</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the union bound over <math id="A6.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\forall t\in[T],\,\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\lesssim\log\frac{T}{\delta}+dr\log(LST)\right)\geq 1-\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≲</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\forall t\in[T],\,\sum_{i=1}^{t}(P_{\widehat{\bm{\Theta}}_{t}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i}))^{2}\lesssim\log\frac{T}{\delta}+dr\log(LST)\right)\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p">which concludes the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma F.6. ‣ F.2 Proof of : MLE Estimator Bound ‣ Appendix F Instantiating Regret Bound of ( ) to GBPM ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof closely follows that of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al. (2024, Lemma 1)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025a, Lemma 3)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the function <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\bm{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\bm{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by the fixed <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Theta}\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Theta}\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we first upper bound its logarithmic moment generating function as</p>
<table id="A6.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex170"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}\exp\!\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}\exp\!\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex171"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Biggl(\sum_{i=1}^{t-1}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}+\log\Bigl(2\,\mathbb{E}_{r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t}}\sqrt{\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})}}\Bigr)\Biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Biggl(\sum_{i=1}^{t-1}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}+\log\Bigl(2\,\mathbb{E}_{r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t}}\sqrt{\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})}}\Bigr)\Biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex172"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Biggl(\sum_{i=1}^{t-1}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}+\log\Bigl(1-H\,\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})\bigr)^{2}\Bigr)\Biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Biggl(\sum_{i=1}^{t-1}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}+\log\Bigl(1-H\,\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})\bigr)^{2}\Bigr)\Biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex173"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Biggl(\sum_{i=1}^{t-1}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}-H\,\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})\bigr)^{2}\Biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Biggl(\sum_{i=1}^{t-1}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}-H\,\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{t}\mid{\bm{z}}_{t})\bigr)^{2}\Biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex174"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\cdots\leq-\sum_{i=1}^{t}H\,\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\bigr)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\cdots\leq-\sum_{i=1}^{t}H\,\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\bigr)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(P\|Q)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P\|Q)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the squared Hellinger distance between probability measures <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as</p>
<table id="A6.Ex175" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(P\|Q)^{2}:=\int_{\Omega}\left(\sqrt{p(z)}-\sqrt{q(z)}\right)^{2}\,d\mu(z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P\|Q)^{2}:=\int_{\Omega}\left(\sqrt{p(z)}-\sqrt{q(z)}\right)^{2}\,d\mu(z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> denoting their respective densities with respect to a base measure <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We continue to lower-bound the Hellinger distance by</p>
<table id="A6.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{t}\Bigl(H\,\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\bigr)\Bigr)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{t}\Bigl(H\,\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\bigr)\Bigr)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex176.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{t}\Bigl(\mathrm{TV}\,\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\bigr)\Bigr)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>TV</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{t}\Bigl(\mathrm{TV}\,\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\bigr)\Bigr)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex177"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\Bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i})\Bigr)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\Bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i})\Bigr)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the inequality uses the fact that for any distribution <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p,q)\geq\mathrm{TV}(p,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p,q)\geq\mathrm{TV}(p,q)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib107" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang, 2023</a>, Theorem B.9)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Then, by <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma G.1 (Martingale Exponential Inequalities; Theorem 13.2 of ( ) ). ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, we obtain for each <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Theta}}\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Theta}}\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex178"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex178.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\!\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)+\log\mathbb{E}\exp\!\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\!\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)+\log\mathbb{E}\exp\!\left(\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}{P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex179"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\sum_{i=1}^{t}H\!\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\bigr)^{2}+\log\!\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\sum_{i=1}^{t}H\!\bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\,\|\,P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}(r_{i}\mid{\bm{z}}_{i})\bigr)^{2}+\log\!\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex180"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\sum_{i=1}^{t}\Bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i})\Bigr)^{2}+\log\!\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\sum_{i=1}^{t}\Bigl(P_{\bm{\Theta}}({\bm{z}}_{i})-P_{\bm{\Theta}_{\star}}({\bm{z}}_{i})\Bigr)^{2}+\log\!\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Auxiliary Lemmas</h2>

<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.1</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Martingale Exponential Inequalities; Theorem 13.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib107" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang (2023)</a></cite>)<span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a sequence of random functions <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{1}(\mathcal{Z}_{1}),\ldots,\xi_{t}(\mathcal{Z}_{t}),\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{1}(\mathcal{Z}_{1}),\ldots,\xi_{t}(\mathcal{Z}_{t}),\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to filtration <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{F}_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{F}_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have for any <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex181" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(\exists n&gt;0:-\sum_{i=1}^{n}\xi_{i}\geq\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{\lambda}+\frac{1}{\lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\mathbb{E}_{Z_{i}^{(y)}}\exp(-\lambda\xi_{i})\right)\leq\delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(\exists n&gt;0:-\sum_{i=1}^{n}\xi_{i}\geq\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{\lambda}+\frac{1}{\lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\mathbb{E}_{Z_{i}^{(y)}}\exp(-\lambda\xi_{i})\right)\leq\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}=(Z_{t}^{(x)},Z_{t}^{(y)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}=(Z_{t}^{(x)},Z_{t}^{(y)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{t}=(Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{t}=(Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.2</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Multiplicative Chernoff Bounds; Corollary 2.18 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib107" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang (2023)</a></cite>)<span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}X=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}X=\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex182"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\bar{X}_{n}\geq(1+\epsilon)\mu\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\bar{X}_{n}\geq(1+\epsilon)\mu\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex182.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\left[\frac{-2n\mu\epsilon^{2}}{2+\epsilon}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\left[\frac{-2n\mu\epsilon^{2}}{2+\epsilon}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex183"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\bar{X}_{n}\leq(1-\epsilon)\mu\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\bar{X}_{n}\leq(1-\epsilon)\mu\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex183.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\left[\frac{-2n\mu\epsilon^{2}}{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\left[\frac{-2n\mu\epsilon^{2}}{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, for <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex184" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(\bar{X}_{n}\geq\mu+\sqrt{\frac{2\mu t}{n}}+\frac{t}{3n}\right)\leq\exp(-t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(\bar{X}_{n}\geq\mu+\sqrt{\frac{2\mu t}{n}}+\frac{t}{3n}\right)\leq\exp(-t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.3</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Elliptical Potential Lemma; Lemma 11 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abbasi-Yadkori et al. (2011)</a></cite>)<span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},\cdots,{\bm{x}}_{T}\in{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},\cdots,{\bm{x}}_{T}\in{\mathcal{B}}^{d}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of vectors and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}_{t}:=\lambda{\bm{I}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}{\bm{x}}_{s}{\bm{x}}_{s}^{\intercal}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊺</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}_{t}:=\lambda{\bm{I}}+\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}{\bm{x}}_{s}{\bm{x}}_{s}^{\intercal}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex185" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}\min\left\{1,\lVert{\bm{x}}_{t}\rVert^{2}_{{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}}\right\}\leq 2d\log\left(1+\frac{X^{2}T}{d\lambda}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}\min\left\{1,\lVert{\bm{x}}_{t}\rVert^{2}_{{\bm{V}}_{t}^{-1}}\right\}\leq 2d\log\left(1+\frac{X^{2}T}{d\lambda}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Future Directions</h2>

<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Relaxing the Feature Diversity Assumption.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our current regret bounds rely on the feature diversity assumption (<a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Feature Map and Diversity). ‣ Feature Diversity. ‣ 2.1 (Self-Play) Interaction Protocol ‣ 2 Problem Setting ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), characterized by the minimum eigenvalue <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>.
While this assumption is standard in the contextual bandits literature that involves either greedy sampling (e.g., algorithms without sophisticated exploration strategies) or high dimensions, it may still be restrictive for general RLHF applications.
Recent works have investigated minimal assumptions required for greedy strategies, such as the local anti-concentration (LAC) property proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib122" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim and Oh (2024)</a></cite>.
Investigating the impact of such relaxed conditions on online RLHF with <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">GBPM</span>  (e.g., whether we can still obtain <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{{\mathcal{O}}(\eta)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">e</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#BF0040">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">η</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}e^{{\mathcal{O}}(\eta)}}</annotation></semantics></math>-free polylogarithmic regret with <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GS</span>) remains an important open question.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Instance-Specific Guarantees for Unregularized Regret.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While our work establishes <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}(\sqrt{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathcal{O}}}(\sqrt{T})</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees for <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">unregularized</span> regret (via <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1 Norm + Skew-Constrained MLE ‣ 4 𝒪̃⁢(𝜂⁢(log𝑇)^2∧√𝑇) via Greedy Sampling ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>), these bounds reflect worst-case hardness.
For instance, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ito et al. (2025)</a></cite> demonstrated that in tabular games with bandit feedback, the Nash regret for the Tsallis-INF algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib81" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tsallis, 1988</a>; <a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abernethy et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zimmert and Seldin, 2021</a>)</cite> scales with the “sparsity” or “entropy” of the NE set, potentially achieving logarithmic regret <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(\log T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(\log T)</annotation></semantics></math> when the NE is unique and deterministic (a pure strategy), and even rates of the form <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{O}}(T^{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{O}}(T^{c})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, depending on the geometry of the set of Nash Equilibria.
Adapting such instance-dependent guarantees to the contextual <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">GBPM</span> setting is non-trivial, even when the link function <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is linear.
Recent advances in “Best-of-Both-Worlds” algorithms for linear contextual bandits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib79" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kuroki et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib80" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kato and Ito, 2025</a>)</cite> may provide a promising starting point.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Computationally Efficient Algorithms.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our current theoretical framework assumes access to a computational oracle for finding the NE (<a href="#Thmoracle3" title="Oracle 3. ‣ Computation Oracles. ‣ 2.3 Regularized NE and Regret Definitions ‣ 2 Problem Setting ‣ Regularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Oracle</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), which may be computationally expensive in practice.
Developing efficient variants of our algorithms is a practical priority.
Promising approaches include leveraging online estimation techniques such as Online Mirror Descent (OMD) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib86" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, minimax optimization techniques such as optimistic OMD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rakhlin and Sridharan, 2013a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Syrgkanis et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025c</a>)</cite>, or reductions to offline/online regression oracles <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib88" title="" class="ltx_ref">Foster and Rakhlin, 2020</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
